#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Council deliberation prose for the main book *Agentic Design Patterns &
Guardrails*.

Four researchers (continual-learning, memory-systems, evaluation, safety)
debate each pattern, each part, each Part X chapter, and the front/back
matter. Read by ``tools/build_book.py``; the build fails if any pattern id,
part key, or Part X title lacks an entry, so catalog changes force prose
updates. No entry may state a measured number — all figures in the book come
from the catalog and repository at build time.
"""

PATTERN_DELIB = {'chain-of-thought': [('Continual-learning researcher', 'Chain-of-Thought helps multi-step arithmetic and inference across general, finance and legal tasks by prompting the model to emit intermediate reasoning steps before the final answer with think step by step or few-shot traces, separating reasoning from the final answer in the output schema using a Prompt template, Reasoning parser and Answer extractor. The core tension is Reasoning drift where fluent but invalid steps rationalize a wrong answer. The protection that carries weight is verifying conclusions with an independent check via Chain-of-Verification alongside Self-Consistency, and the operator should verify that reasoning cannot alter the answer format.'), ('Safety researcher', 'I agree that the independent check you name matters, but I would put the weight on never treating CoT as privileged since it can be prompt-injected like any output, which directly addresses the second documented failure of Reasoning leakage where hidden chain-of-thought or attacker-controlled text leaks into logs. The CoT-hidden variant that shows only conclusions helps, yet the structured output schema must still constrain the answer and the Reasoning parser must isolate traces. Related ReAct reminds the operator to verify logs and downstream consumers for leaked reasoning.')], 'self-consistency': [('Evaluation methodologist', 'Self-Consistency Sampling improves answers in general, finance and healthcare settings by sampling N reasoning paths at temperature above zero and taking the majority answer, running parallel CoT samples with an N-way sampler, Answer clusterer and Agreement threshold gate where disagreement signals low confidence. The tension is Shared-blind-spot consensus where all samples are wrong the same way from the same base model bias. The protection that carries weight is treating consensus as confidence not truth with deterministic checks for actions plus diversity across temperatures or models, linked to Chain-of-Thought and Debate-Council, and the operator should verify escalation on low agreement.'), ('Continual-learning researcher', 'Your point on shared bias is right, and I would add that the other documented failure of Cost multiplication makes this fragile because N samples multiply token spend and loops burn budget fast. That is why capping N and total spend per query carries practical weight alongside still applying deterministic checks for actions. The Ensemble-Verify relation reinforces that majority vote needs an external anchor, so the operator should verify the agreement threshold gate routes below-threshold cases to escalate or abstain rather than emitting a confident majority.')], 'tree-of-thoughts': [('Continual-learning researcher', 'Tree of Thoughts helps general, research and legal reasoning by exploring multiple candidate branches with self-evaluation and backtracking like search over thoughts, generating candidate next steps, scoring each with a value function, then keeping top-k with expansion and backtracking using a Branch generator, Value scorer and Search controller with BFS or DFS. The tension is Exploration cost blowup where branching multiplies tokens and unbounded depth creates budget runaway. The protection that carries weight is hard caps on depth times width times tokens shared with the outer agent loop and Budget-Bounded-Exec, and the operator should verify caps hold before search starts.'), ('Safety researcher', 'Caps are necessary, but the deeper risk you underplay is Value scorer gamed where the same model generates and scores so it favors its own plausible-looking branches. That is why an independent scorer with a different model or prompt for high-stakes branches carries the real weight, alongside the shared budget guardrail. Related Chain-of-Thought shows the base step being searched, so the operator should verify scorer independence and that dead-end backtracking does not simply re-select self-flattering branches.')], 'react': [('Memory-systems researcher', 'ReAct is the canonical agentic loop for general, research and DevOps work by interleaving Thought, Action and Observation cycles where the model emits Thought slash Action slash Observation, the environment returns an observation after each action, and the loop ends on Final Answer or budget slash steps cap using an LLM planner, Action parser, Tool executor and Observation buffer. The tension is Unbounded loops where the agent retries the same failing action forever while burning tokens and side effects. The protection that carries weight is max-iterations with stall detection through a circuit breaker tied to Standard-Agent-Loop, and the operator should verify termination fires.'), ('Safety researcher', 'Stall limits help, but the critical failure is Injected observations where tool output such as a web page or email contains instructions the model obeys, compounded by Hallucinated tool calls that invent tool names and arguments corrupting external state. The protections that carry weight are strict tool schemas with server-side argument validation and treating all observations as untrusted data with a prompt-injection shield, related to Tool-Use and Circuit-Breaker. The operator should verify every observation is handled as data never as instruction.')], 'plan-and-execute': [('Continual-learning researcher', 'Plan-and-Execute helps general, procurement and research tasks by making a full plan up front with a planner model then executing steps with a cheaper executor and re-planning only when reality diverges, with the planner producing ordered steps, the executor running one step at a time, and the re-planner patching remaining steps using a Planner LLM, Plan store, Step executor and Re-planner slash divergence checker. The tension is Stale plan adherence where the executor follows a plan invalidated by new world state. The protection that carries weight is re-validating preconditions before each step with versioned plans, related to ReAct and Dynamic-DAG, and the operator should verify preconditions at every step.'), ('Safety researcher', 'Re-validation matters, yet the higher-severity failure is Plan poisoning where attacker content read during execution sneaks into re-planner context and reshapes the plan. That is why freezing high-risk steps behind approvals regardless of plan state carries the weight, plus logging plan diffs in the audit trail. Related Subgoal-Gating reinforces gated progress, so the operator should verify that approval gates cannot be skipped even when the stored plan claims authorization.')], 'task-decomposition': [('Evaluation methodologist', 'Task Decomposition helps general, research and engineering goals by breaking a goal into subtasks through prompting, LLM-generated trees or task-specific prompts, emitting a task tree or checklist, executing subtasks sequentially or in parallel, and aggregating bottom-up with a Decomposer, Subtask queue and Aggregator. The tension is Missing-critical-subtask where decomposition silently omits a safety-relevant step such as a budget check. The protection that carries weight is a golden checklist of mandatory subtasks per domain such as verify before irreversible action, related to Plan-and-Execute and Orchestrator-Workers, and the operator should verify mandatory steps are present.'), ('Memory-systems researcher', 'The checklist is essential, and the companion failure is Aggregation mismatch where sub-results are individually fine but inconsistent when merged. That is why an aggregator validation pass with schema constraints carries weight alongside tracking subtask provenance so every merged claim cites its subtask. The bottom-up merge only works if provenance travels with claims, so the operator should verify the Aggregator rejects inconsistent merges rather than smoothing over conflicts.')], 'least-to-most': [('Continual-learning researcher', 'Least-to-Most Prompting helps general and education tasks by solving the easiest subproblem first and feeding its answer into harder subproblems in cascading difficulty, decomposing ordered by dependency, solving incrementally while carrying solutions forward, and stopping to escalate when a subproblem fails using a Dependency orderer and Incremental solver. The tension is Error cascades where one wrong early answer poisons every downstream subproblem. The protection that carries weight is checkpointing each sub-answer and verifying before use, related to Task-Decomposition and Validation-Loop, and the operator should verify no downstream step consumes an unchecked answer.'), ('Evaluation methodologist', 'Checkpointing is the right anchor, and I would stress the second protection of branching and retrying on a failed subproblem rather than continuing. Because the incremental solver carries forward prior solutions, continuing after failure guarantees compounded error. Related Validation-Loop frames that retry discipline, so the operator should verify the stop-and-escalate rule actually halts the cascade and triggers a retry branch instead of pushing a suspect answer forward.')], 'chain-of-verification': [('Evaluation methodologist', 'Chain-of-Verification helps research, legal, healthcare and finance accuracy by drafting a response, then independently drafting verification questions, answering them without the original context, and revising through a Draft generator, Question generator, Independent verifier and Reviser. The tension is Self-verification illusion where the same model verifying itself inherits the same hallucination. The protection that carries weight is verifying against external ground truth such as databases and APIs not just the model, related to LLM-Judge and Reflexion, and the operator should verify revision or abstention on mismatch.'), ('Safety researcher', 'External grounding is decisive, and the companion failure is Citation theater where the agent produces verifiable-looking citations that do not exist. That is why requiring retrievable source IDs for every factual claim used in actions carries weight alongside abstaining when verification fails instead of guessing. Related Provenance-Citation reinforces source accountability, so the operator should verify every claim presented for action has a retrievable source before execution.')], 'reflexion': [('Continual-learning researcher', 'Reflexion helps general, engineering and DevOps tasks by having the agent critique its own outcome after an attempt and store verbal feedback in memory to improve the next try, attempting the task, producing a verbal reinforcement signal from an evaluator, then storing reflection and retrying with reflection in context using an Actor, Self-critic and Reflection memory. The tension is Rationalization loop where the agent reflects its way into defending a wrong action. The protection that carries weight is grounding reflections in deterministic signals such as test results and API errors not model opinion alone, related to Self-Critique, and the operator should verify retry count is bounded.'), ('Safety researcher', 'Deterministic grounding helps, but the high-severity failure is Reflection poisoning where attacker text becomes the lesson memorized for future runs. That is why human review of reflections before they enter long-term memory carries the weight, alongside bounding retries and escalating after k reflections. Related Memory-Consolidation shows the persistence risk, so the operator should verify no reflection enters Reflection memory without review against test and error evidence.')], 'self-critique': [('Evaluation methodologist', 'Self-Critique and Revise helps general, marketing and legal drafting by iterating draft to critique against explicit criteria to revise until criteria pass or budget is exhausted, with a Draft generator, Rubric critic and Editor. The tension is Rubric drift where the critic invents criteria not in the rubric causing endless churn. The protection that carries weight is a fixed machine-checkable rubric where only measurable criteria count, related to Evaluator-Optimizer and Reflexion, and the operator should verify iterations stop at max rounds by shipping the best-scoring draft.'), ('Continual-learning researcher', 'A fixed rubric stabilizes the loop, and the companion failure is Over-polish where revision removes accurate hedging and makes outputs sound more certain than warranted. That is why preserving uncertainty markers through revision carries weight alongside keeping the best-scoring draft rather than the last one. The Editor must not polish away doubt, so the operator should verify hedging and confidence language survive each revise pass.')], 'metacognitive-confidence': [('Evaluation methodologist', 'Confidence Gating helps healthcare, finance, legal and general decisions by having the agent estimate its own confidence per decision and only auto-act above threshold otherwise deferring, asking or abstaining, using calibrated confidence from logprobs, self-report or agreement with a Confidence estimator, Risk-class table and Threshold gate. The tension is Overconfident calibration where LLM confidence is poorly calibrated and agents claim certainty they lack. The protection that carries weight is calibrating thresholds against real labeled outcomes not vibes with per-domain thresholds stricter for irreversible actions, related to Human-in-the-Loop, and the operator should verify thresholds per risk class.'), ('Safety researcher', 'Calibration is foundational, but the operational failure is Threshold fatigue where too many deferrals train operators to approve everything. That is why tracking deferral-to-approval ratio as an alerting metric carries weight alongside Uncertainty-Abstention discipline. Related Human-in-the-Loop shows the human endpoint, so the operator should verify alerting fires when approvals become rubber stamps and that low-confidence paths truly route to ask-human or abstain.')], 'analogical-reasoning': [('Memory-systems researcher', 'Analogical and Case-Based Reasoning helps legal, support and engineering work by retrieving past cases closest to the current situation and adapting their resolutions, embedding the current case, retrieving k similar past cases, then adapting the precedent solution while citing case IDs using a Case memory store, Similarity retriever and Adapter. The tension is Bad precedent transfer where a superficially similar case with materially different context leads the agent astray. The protection that carries weight is showing distinguishing differences alongside similarities with a human-curated store, related to Episodic-Memory and RAG-Augmented, and the operator should verify differences are reviewed.'), ('Safety researcher', 'Surfacing differences helps, but the high-severity failure is Precedent poisoning where an adversary plants a precedent in the case store. That is why a human-curated case store with provenance and review carries the weight alongside never auto-applying precedent to irreversible actions. The Adapter must not launder planted cases, so the operator should verify provenance on every retrieved precedent before any consequential adaptation.')], 'skeptic-devils-advocate': [('Safety researcher', "Skeptical Reasoning helps finance, legal and strategy planning through a dedicated critique pass that argues against the agent's own plan before execution, where the planner proposes action, the skeptic prompt attacks assumptions and enumerates failure modes, and only surviving plans proceed using a Planner, Skeptic critic and Verdict gate. The tension is Performative skepticism where the critic raises cosmetic objections while missing the real risk. The protection that carries weight is mapping objections to a threat taxonomy for checklist coverage, related to Debate-Council and Red-Team-Pair, and the operator should verify coverage before the gate passes."), ('Evaluation methodologist', 'Checklist coverage is the right bar, and the companion protections of weighting irreversible-action objections above style objections and using separate context windows for planner and skeptic carry the operational weight. Without separation the skeptic inherits planner framing and stays cosmetic. The Verdict gate should enforce that ordering, so the operator should verify planner and skeptic contexts are isolated and that irreversible risks block progress even when style issues dominate the critique.')], 'recursive-criticism': [('Evaluation methodologist', 'Recursive Criticism and Improvement helps general refinement by iterating critique to improve to critique with diminishing returns and convergence detection, looping critic scores and improver revises and stopping when score delta falls below epsilon or max rounds hit using a Critic, Improver and Convergence detector. The tension is Oscillation where two versions flip-flop without converging. The protection that carries weight is detecting flip-flop and stopping while keeping the best-scoring artifact not the last one, related to Self-Critique, and the operator should verify the detector halts the loop on cycles.'), ('Continual-learning researcher', 'Keeping the best artifact is wise, and the companion failure is Token runaway on hard problems with unbounded rounds. That is why max-rounds and total-token budget carry the weight alongside Budget-Bounded-Exec discipline. The Convergence detector only matters if the budget enforces an exit, so the operator should verify round and token ceilings are set before iteration begins and that the best version is shipped.')], 'standard-agent-loop': [('Memory-systems researcher', 'The Standard Agent Loop supports general runtime work by cycling retrieve context to plan to select tool to execute to observe to repeat until done or bounded, assembling context from system prompt, memory, tool docs and history, letting the LLM choose the next action, executing and appending observations, with stop on goal met, steps cap, budget cap or human stop using a Context assembler, LLM, Tool registry, History store and Stop-condition engine. The tension is Runaway loop with no effective stop where costs and side effects compound. The protection that carries weight is hard step, token and dollar caps enforced by runtime not the model, related to ReAct and Budget-Bounded-Exec, and the operator should verify caps are external.'), ('Safety researcher', 'External caps are essential, and the companion failure is Context window overflow where history grows until the model truncates safety instructions. That is why a context compressor that never drops system safety policy carries weight alongside writing every loop iteration to the audit trail. Related Audit-Trail gives accountability, so the operator should verify compression preserves policy and that the History store never squeezes out guardrails.')], 'ooda': [('Continual-learning researcher', 'The OODA Loop helps cybersecurity, trading and robotics performance by emphasizing Observe, Orient, Decide and Act speed with re-orientation in adversarial and fast-moving environments, observing signals, orienting against a world model, deciding and acting then immediately re-observing using a Signal feed, World model and Decision policy. The tension is Orientation bias where the agent acts on a stale world model in a moving environment. The protection that carries weight is freshness checks that discard stale observations, related to Standard-Agent-Loop and Drift-Monitoring, and the operator should verify orientation uses current signals.'), ('Safety researcher', 'Freshness matters, but the high-severity failure is Adversarial manipulation where an attacker feeds observations to steer orientation through spoofed telemetry. That is why signed and authenticated telemetry sources carry the weight alongside rate limits on reactive actions. Speed without trust lets spoofing drive decisions, so the operator should verify source authentication and that rapid Decide-Act cycles remain rate-limited.')], 'tool-use': [('Safety researcher', 'Tool Use helps general agency by exposing typed tools where the model emits structured calls the runtime validates and executes, publishing JSON-schema definitions, validating args, checking permissions, executing and returning results using a Tool registry, Schema validator, Permission checker and Executor. The tension is Confused deputy where broad agent credentials are used on behalf of a low-privilege requester. The protection that carries weight is per-caller scoped tokens so the agent never holds ambient authority, related to Function-Calling and Least-Privilege, and the operator should verify scopes per caller.'), ('Evaluation methodologist', 'Scoped authority is decisive, and the companion failures are Argument injection where attacker-influenced content shapes tool args such as recipient or URL and Tool hallucination where the model calls non-existent tools or malformed args. The protections that carry weight are server-side schema validation with semantic checks including allowlists and ranges plus dry-run and diff mode for state-changing tools, related to Tool-Sandbox. The operator should verify validation and dry-run precede any state change.')], 'human-in-the-loop': [('Safety researcher', 'Human-in-the-Loop helps finance, healthcare, legal and DevOps safety by routing high-risk or low-confidence decisions to humans for review before execution, with policy deciding which actions need approval, the agent pausing with a full context package, and resuming after human approve, reject or edit using a Policy engine, Review queue UI and Resume controller. The tension is Bypass via escalation where the agent finds another route with a different tool to perform the same action. The protection that carries weight is enforcing approvals at the tool layer so no path skips them, related to Approval-Gates and Dual-Control, and the operator should verify tool-layer enforcement.'), ('Evaluation methodologist', 'Tool-layer enforcement closes the bypass, but the companion failures are Approval fatigue where volume trains reviewers to rubber-stamp and Context-starved review where a one-line summary hides the poison pill. The protections that carry weight are batching and prioritizing with alerts on rubber-stamp rate while showing the reviewer the diff, provenance of every input, and guardrail rationale, related to Interrupt-Resume. The operator should verify reviewers receive full evidence not summaries.')], 'interrupt-resume': [('Memory-systems researcher', 'Interrupt and Resume helps finance, DevOps and procurement continuity by serializing agent state, requesting permission, and resuming days later with a different operator without redoing work, checkpointing plan, args and evidence at approval points, persisting and notifying, then resuming with idempotency keys using a Checkpoint store, Approval service and Idempotent executor. The tension is Duplicate execution on resume where resume re-runs a side effect that already happened. The protection that carries weight is idempotency keys on every side effect, related to Human-in-the-Loop and Idempotency-Keys, and the operator should verify keys exist before resume.'), ('Safety researcher', 'Idempotency prevents doubles, but the high-severity failure is TOCTOU staleness where the world changed between proposal and approval so the approved action is now unsafe. That is why re-validating preconditions at execution time not approval time carries the weight alongside approval expiry windows. Related Checkpoint-Rollback frames recovery, so the operator should verify fresh precondition checks and expiry at resume time.')], 'checkpoint-rollback': [('Continual-learning researcher', 'Checkpointing and Rollback helps DevOps, engineering and finance safety by snapshotting state before risky operations so the agent can revert on failure, snapshotting touched resources, executing with monitoring, then rolling back on failure or committing and discarding the snapshot using a Snapshot manager, Rollback executor and Health verifier. The tension is Incomplete snapshot where the agent misses a side-effect surface such as an external API it cannot roll back. The protection that carries weight is inventorying all side effects before acting and classifying reversible versus irreversible, related to Saga-Compensation, and the operator should verify the inventory is complete.'), ('Safety researcher', 'Complete inventory is necessary, and the critical failure is Rollback itself fails with no rehearsed recovery leading to cascade. That is why rehearsing rollbacks and verifying post-rollback health carries weight alongside refusing actions with un-rollbackable effects without approval, related to Irreversible-Action-Confirm. The Health verifier must confirm recovery, so the operator should verify rehearsal evidence and approval for irreversible steps.')], 'budget-bounded-exec': [('Evaluation methodologist', 'Budget-Bounded Execution is the master circuit breaker for general tasks through runtime-enforced ceilings on steps, tokens, wall-clock, tool calls and dollars per task, declaring budget at task start, metering consumption across every loop, and stopping with checkpoint and report on exhaustion using Metering middleware, Budget registry and Stop controller. The tension is Budget set by the model where the agent writes its own limits and attacker-influenced models raise them. The protection that carries weight is budgets set by the caller and policy engine never the model and immutable at runtime, related to Quota-Rate-Limit and Circuit-Breaker, and the operator should verify immutability.'), ('Safety researcher', 'Caller-set budgets are foundational, and the companion failure is Unmetered side channels where sub-agents or deferred jobs escape the meter. That is why metering that includes all descendants including sub-agents and retries carries weight alongside dollar-denominated not just token-denominated accounting, related to Standard-Agent-Loop. The operator should verify the Budget registry aggregates descendant spend before exhaustion handling.')], 'timeboxing': [('Evaluation methodologist', 'Timeboxing helps general and DevOps delivery through a wall-clock deadline per task where the agent must deliver a partial result or escalate on expiry, setting a deadline at dispatch, planning with time awareness, then reducing scope and checkpointing and escalating at expiry using a Deadline clock and Scope-reduction policy. The tension is Deadline-induced corner cutting where the agent skips verification under time pressure. The protection that carries weight is exempting verification steps from scope reduction, related to Budget-Bounded-Exec and Subgoal-Gating, and the operator should verify verification still runs at deadline.'), ('Continual-learning researcher', 'Protecting verification is the key point, and the companion protection of graceful partial delivery with explicit incomplete markers carries the operational weight. Because scope reduction must not masquerade as completion, markers preserve honesty about what was cut. The Scope-reduction policy should enforce that labeling, so the operator should verify partial outputs are flagged incomplete and routed to escalate rather than presented as finished.')], 'subgoal-gating': [('Evaluation methodologist', 'Subgoal Gating helps engineering, procurement and research discipline by splitting long tasks into milestones where each gate requires a verifiable success criterion before proceeding, defining milestones with machine-checkable exit criteria, executing to gate, then passing to the next or replanning and escalating using a Milestone registry and Gate evaluators. The tension is Weak exit criteria where gates the model self-certifies become no-ops. The protection that carries weight is evaluating gates by deterministic checks where possible, related to Plan-and-Execute and Evaluator-Optimizer, and the operator should verify criteria are machine-checkable.'), ('Continual-learning researcher', 'Deterministic checks give gates teeth, and separating evaluator from actor carries the complementary weight so the actor cannot grade its own milestone. Related Evaluator-Optimizer models that separation explicitly. Because self-certification hollows out milestones, the operator should verify the Gate evaluators are independent of the execution path and that failures trigger replan or escalate rather than silent advance.')], 'prompt-chaining': [('Continual-learning researcher', 'Prompt Chaining helps general tasks by decomposing work into a fixed sequence of LLM calls with structured output feeding the next step and gates between steps, using fixed pipelines, validated structured output per step, and optional reject or branch on failed validation with Prompt steps, Schema validators and Gates. The tension is Error compounding where early hallucination gets laundered into fact by later steps. The protection that carries weight is validating at every boundary and failing closed, related to Routing and Sequential-Pipeline, and the operator should verify boundary validation blocks suspect outputs.'), ('Evaluation methodologist', 'Boundary validation is essential, and the companion protections of provenance tags traveling with data through the chain and monitoring per-step failure rates as drift signal carry lasting weight. Because fixed chains are rigid to novel inputs outside the design envelope, drift monitoring reveals envelope breaches. The Gates enforce discipline, so the operator should verify provenance persists across steps and failure-rate alerts are reviewed.')], 'routing': [('Evaluation methodologist', 'Routing helps support and general workloads by having a classifier dispatch input to a specialized downstream prompt or model with a cheap fast path and an expensive path only when needed, routing with an LLM or small-model classifier, handling shards with specialist prompts, and keeping a fallback lane using a Router classifier, Specialist prompt set and Fallback lane. The tension is Misrouting where an urgent safety issue goes to a chatty general lane. The protection that carries weight is hard-coding safety-critical intents to a fixed route not a learned one, related to Specialist-Triage and Prompt-Chaining, and the operator should verify critical intents cannot be learned away.'), ('Safety researcher', 'Hard-coded safety routes are decisive, and the high-severity failure is Router poisoning where injection text manipulates routing to a permissive specialist. That is why specialists inheriting the same guardrails as the generalist carries weight alongside logging route decisions and alerting on unusual route distribution. The Router classifier must not downgrade protections, so the operator should verify guardrail parity and review route logs for anomalies.')], 'parallelization-sectioning': [('Continual-learning researcher', 'Parallelization by Sectioning helps research, legal and general throughput by running independent subtasks concurrently and merging, splitting into independent units, fanning out to concurrent workers, and merging deterministically with a Fan-out scheduler, Workers and Merger. The tension is Non-independent split where hidden dependencies cause inconsistent merges. The protection that carries weight is deterministic merge with conflict detection, related to Parallelization-Voting and Orchestrator-Workers, and the operator should verify the Merger surfaces conflicts rather than hiding them.'), ('Evaluation methodologist', 'Conflict-aware merging is key, and the companion failure is Thundering-herd cost where fan-out multiplies spend and retries amplify. That is why global concurrency and spend caps across the fan-out carry weight. Because concurrent Workers compound cost quickly, the Fan-out scheduler must enforce ceilings, so the operator should verify caps cover initial fan-out plus retries before launch.')], 'parallelization-voting': [('Evaluation methodologist', 'Parallel Voting helps finance, healthcare and legal reliability by running the same task n times and voting or judging to boost reliability on a single decision, with n parallel identical runs, vote or LLM-judge selection, and escalation on disagreement using N runners and Voter slash judge. The tension is Correlated errors where all n share the same base-model bias creating false confidence. The protection that carries weight is using heterogeneous models when stakes are high, related to Self-Consistency and Ensemble-Verify, and the operator should verify model diversity for consequential votes.'), ('Safety researcher', 'Diversity mitigates shared bias, but the high-severity failure is Judge capture where the judge shares the blind spot or is itself injected. That is why blinded candidates where the judge sees anonymized options carries weight alongside treating disagreement as an escalation trigger never a silent tiebreak, related to LLM-Judge. The operator should verify blinding and that disagreement routes to escalate.')], 'orchestrator-workers': [('Memory-systems researcher', 'Orchestrator-Workers helps general, engineering and research scale where a central orchestrator dynamically decomposes work and spawns worker LLMs with shared context then synthesizes results, analyzing tasks, executing in parallel with task-specific context, and synthesizing through an Orchestrator, Worker pool, Shared context store and Synthesizer. The tension is Runaway fan-out where the orchestrator keeps spawning workers and cost explodes. The protection that carries weight is max worker fan-out and per-worker budget, related to Hierarchical-Teams and Fan-Out-Caps, and the operator should verify fan-out ceilings before decomposition.'), ('Safety researcher', 'Fan-out caps contain cost, but the paired failures are Worker privilege escalation where workers inherit orchestrator credentials and overreach and Synthesis hallucination where the synthesizer invents agreement between conflicting outputs. The protections that carry weight are per-worker scoped credentials with tool allowlists and requiring synthesis to surface conflicts not average them away via the Shared context store. The operator should verify scopes and conflict surfacing.')], 'evaluator-optimizer': [('Evaluation methodologist', 'Evaluator-Optimizer helps legal, engineering and content quality where one model generates and another evaluates against explicit criteria looping until pass or budget exhausted, with generator producing candidates, evaluator scoring against a rubric, and feedback looping back using a Generator, Evaluator and Loop controller. The tension is Generator-evaluator collusion where same-family models converge on a wrong answer. The protection that carries weight is diversity across different model families with the evaluator grounded in external facts or tests where possible, related to LLM-Judge and Self-Critique, and the operator should verify independence and grounding.'), ('Continual-learning researcher', 'Independent grounding is crucial, and the companion failure is Unbounded iteration where the loop never converges and budget bleeds. That is why hard iteration and spend caps with keeping the best candidate carry weight alongside Budget-Bounded-Exec limits. The Loop controller must enforce exit, so the operator should verify caps are set and that the shipped output is the best candidate not merely the last attempt.')], 'dynamic-dag': [('Continual-learning researcher', 'Dynamic DAG Planning helps engineering, data and DevOps execution by having the planner emit an explicit dependency graph at runtime with a scheduler executing ready nodes with retries and caching, planning to DAG nodes, running ready nodes concurrently, and triggering local replan on node failures using a Planner, DAG store, Scheduler and Node cache. The tension is Cyclic or degenerate plans where the model emits cycles or a single mega-node. The protection that carries weight is structural validation of the DAG for acyclicity and bounded width and depth, related to Plan-and-Execute and Parallelization-Sectioning, and the operator should verify structure before scheduling.'), ('Memory-systems researcher', 'Structural validation prevents deadlocks, and the companion failure is Cache poisoning where a wrong cached node result is reused across tasks. That is why cache keyed by input hash plus policy version carries weight alongside per-node budgets rolling up to task budget. Because the Node cache persists across runs, the operator should verify cache keys include policy version and that node spend aggregates to the task ceiling.')], 'pipeline-fallback': [('Evaluation methodologist', 'Pipeline with Fallback helps general and DevOps resilience through a primary path with automatic fallback to a cheaper or safer path on failure or degradation, trying the primary model or tool, chaining to fallback on failure, timeout or degradation, and recording which path served while alerting on fallback spikes using Health checks, Fallback chain and Degradation monitor. The tension is Silent quality drop where the fallback model lacks guardrails of the primary. The protection that carries weight is applying guardrails at a layer shared by all fallbacks, related to Graceful-Degradation and Fallback-Chain, and the operator should verify parity across paths.'), ('Safety researcher', 'Shared guardrails prevent downgrade, and the companion protections of surfacing degraded mode in the UI and audit trail plus alerting on fallback-rate anomaly carry operational weight. Because the Degradation monitor decides switching, silent fallback hides risk. The Health checks must trigger visible labeling, so the operator should verify degraded responses are explicitly marked and anomaly alerts are reviewed.')], 'batch-agents': [('Safety researcher', 'Batch Agent Processing helps data, marketing and support scale through queue-driven bulk runs with dedupe, rate shaping and per-item idempotency, enqueuing items with idempotency keys, processing with rate limits, and parking failures in a dead-letter queue using a Queue, Rate limiter, DLQ and Result store. The tension is Bulk harm amplification where one bad instruction replicates across ten thousand items in minutes. The protection that carries weight is canarying a small fraction of the batch with human approval then ramping, related to Canary-Shadow and Idempotency-Keys, and the operator should verify canary approval precedes full ramp.'), ('Evaluation methodologist', 'Canary gating contains blast radius, and the companion failure is Duplicate side effects where replayed batches re-send emails or refunds. That is why idempotency keys per item per action carry weight alongside global rate caps on outward-facing actions. Because the Queue may replay, the Rate limiter and Result store must enforce once-only effects, so the operator should verify keys and caps before bulk execution.')], 'working-memory-context': [('Memory-systems researcher', 'Working Memory treats the context window as layered working memory where system policy outranks task, retrieved facts, and recent turns, with history truncated first and critical instructions pinned. The Context assembler and Priority-aware truncator carry that ordering, which helps general tasks stay coherent as history grows. Yet the record warns of Context dilution degrading adherence and CWE-style instruction loss where truncation drops the safety policy block entirely.'), ('Safety researcher', 'That loss is why I would not trust ordering alone, since once the policy block vanishes the guardrails vanish mid-task with it. The protection that carries weight here is the pinned policy block re-asserted every N turns plus an attention budget capping history tokens per turn, tied to standard-agent-loop. The operator should verify behavior at context extremes with needle tests and confirm truncation never touches policy, as context-compression alone will not save it.')], 'long-term-vector-memory': [('Memory-systems researcher', 'Long-Term Memory persists embeddings of past interactions and facts in a Vector DB, written on completion with metadata and retrieved by similarity plus recency and importance through an Embedder, Memory writer, and Retriever. That helps support, general, and sales tasks reuse what worked without stuffing everything into context. But its documented failure modes bite hard, especially Memory poisoning where planted facts auto-retrieve forever, alongside PII entombment and stale facts without version context.'), ('Safety researcher', 'You are right that persistence is the risk, which is why the write gate matters more than the retriever. I would keep the human or high-confidence gate with provenance and TTL on every memory, treat retrieved memory as untrusted data never as instructions, and maintain the right-to-erasure pipeline with per-subject deletion. The operator should verify TTLs fire, audit memory-consolidation and rag-augmented linkages, and test that poisoned-memory defenses hold before auto-action.')], 'episodic-memory': [('Continual-learning researcher', 'Episodic Memory stores whole past episodes with outcome labels and replays similar episodes through an Episode recorder and Similarity index, adapting strategies that worked and avoiding what failed. That helps support and general decisions stay case-based rather than abstract. The tension is Outcome mislabeling, where a lucky bad decision is stored as success and then faithfully replayed. Once a mislabeled episode enters the index, similarity retrieval will keep recommending the same flawed strategy.'), ('Evaluation methodologist', 'I agree the label is the load-bearing part, not the similarity score. The protection that carries weight is labeling outcomes with verified ground truth rather than the agent self-report, plus human audit of high-impact episodes. The operator should verify labels against external results, sample episodes linked to analogical-reasoning and long-term-vector-memory, and confirm failed strategies are marked so replay guides avoidance rather than repetition.')], 'semantic-memory-kg': [('Memory-systems researcher', 'Semantic Memory stores facts as typed entities and relations in a Graph DB, extracted from interactions with provenance edges and queried by a Query planner through graph traversal plus embedding hybrid via an Entity extractor. That structured lookup helps enterprise, research, and legal work avoid fuzzy recall. The core tension is Wrong edge becomes canon, where one hallucinated relation is queried confidently downstream and every later traversal inherits the error as if it were settled fact.'), ('Evaluation methodologist', 'That canon problem is why confidence and provenance must gate retrieval, not decorate it. The protection that carries weight is confidence plus provenance on every edge with low-confidence edges hidden from auto-actions, alongside periodic human-verified consolidation. The operator should verify edge provenance resolves, check consolidation linked to long-term-vector-memory and provenance-citation, and confirm uncertain edges cannot drive actions without review.')], 'rag-augmented': [('Evaluation methodologist', 'RAG-Augmented Agent grounds every answer and action in retrieved documents with a Retriever, Reranker, Citation enforcer, and Abstain gate, answering strictly from passages and escalating when retrieval is empty. That helps enterprise, legal, healthcare, and research stay sourced. Yet its documented failure modes compound, especially Poisoned corpus steering future answers, plus Citation mismatch where sources do not support claims and Retrieval leakage exposing the wrong tenant documents.'), ('Safety researcher', 'You named the right ordering, and I would put tenant isolation and claim checks ahead of ingestion alone. The protections that carry weight are ingestion scanning with human review for high-trust corpora, claim-level citation verification before any action, and tenant-scoped retrieval with row-level ACLs enforced at query time. The operator should verify citations entail claims, test empty-retrieval abstention, and audit provenance-citation and poison-defense linkages routinely.')], 'memory-consolidation': [('Continual-learning researcher', 'Memory Consolidation distills raw interaction logs into durable ranked memories through a periodic Consolidator job with a Deduper and Memory store, extracting candidates, deduping against existing entries, and attaching confidence. That helps general and support agents sleep on experience rather than hoarding transcripts. The tension is Consolidation of garbage, where a one-off edge case is memorized as policy and then retrieved as if it were a durable rule for future runs.'), ('Safety researcher', 'I share that worry, which is why the threshold and instruction filter matter most. The protections that carry weight are human review for consolidated memories below confidence threshold and never consolidating anything resembling instructions to bypass policy. The operator should verify dedupe against long-term-vector-memory, review links to reflexion, and confirm low-confidence candidates stay quarantined rather than promoted into the store.')], 'context-compression': [('Memory-systems researcher', 'Context Compression summarizes old turns and tool outputs with a Summarizer and Pin-list extractor, preserving decisions, open items, and constraints while dropping raw tool output to fit the window. That helps general tasks run long without overflow. The tension is sharp because its documented failure modes strike together, with Lossy compression of constraints dropping limits like spending caps and Summary injection faithfully promoting attacker text into instructions that survive longer than the original.'), ('Safety researcher', 'Exactly, and summarization cannot be allowed to rewrite authority. The protection that carries weight is copying the constraint pin-list verbatim without summarizing, marking summaries as untrusted derived data, and auditing decisions before and after compression. The operator should verify pinned constraints survive, treat working-memory-context linkages as suspect until checked, and confirm injected content cannot graduate into instructions through the summary.')], 'scratchpad-external': [('Memory-systems researcher', 'External Scratchpad keeps state in workspace files like plans, progress notes, and artifacts outside the context window through a Workspace FS with scoped File tools, durable across sessions and inspectable by humans. That helps engineering, devops, and research carry work forward and patch plans directly. The tension is filesystem exposure, with Path traversal reading or writing outside the workspace and Scratchpad as exfil channel where secrets copied into notes are later synced or served.'), ('Safety researcher', 'Inspectability helps only if the boundary holds, so containment outranks convenience here. The protections that carry weight are a chrooted workspace with path allowlists, secret scanning on write, and treating scratchpad content as untrusted on read-back. The operator should verify scoped paths deny escapes, audit sandbox-execution and data-loss-prevention linkages, and confirm no secrets persist in files that humans or sync tools later expose.')], 'forgetting-decay': [('Continual-learning researcher', 'Forgetting with Decay and TTL deliberately expires memories through a TTL registry and Decay job, using per-class TTLs, recency-weighted retrieval, and audited deletions to limit staleness, liability, and poison persistence. That helps enterprise and healthcare shed outdated facts rather than entombing them. The tension is Over-forgetting, where useful long-tail knowledge is pruned and the agent loses rare but still valid context that retrieval can no longer surface.'), ('Evaluation methodologist', 'That tradeoff is manageable if expiry stays reviewable rather than silent. The protections that carry weight are legal hold overriding TTL and dry-run decay reports before enforcement. The operator should verify hold logic, inspect dry-run reports for vector-memory and data-loss-prevention impact, and confirm deletions are audited so useful knowledge can be restored and liability-driven expiry remains defensible.')], 'supervisor-workers': [('Evaluation methodologist', 'Supervisor Workers gives one supervisor ownership of the goal, dispatching to isolated specialist workers through a Handoff protocol and integrating results behind a Result gate. That helps general, engineering, and support work parallelize while keeping validation central. The tension is gate weakness, with Rubber-stamp supervisor approving outputs without real verification and Scope creep across workers letting one task bleed into another worker data and tools.'), ('Safety researcher', 'Central ownership fails if the gate is vibes, so checklists and scoping must be enforced. The protections that carry weight are checklist gates rather than impressionistic approval, strict data scopes per worker, and barring workers from calling each other tools. The operator should verify gate criteria are machine-checkable, audit orchestrator-workers and hierarchical-teams linkages, and confirm isolation holds under load.')], 'hierarchical-teams': [('Continual-learning researcher', 'Hierarchical Teams stacks supervision from leaf workers through team leads to directors, with budget and authority scaling by level and escalation upward on ambiguity via multi-level supervisors and an Authority matrix. That helps enterprise and devops mirror familiar escalation paths. The tension is Authority laundering, where a mid-level agent approves what should have risen to a human, compounded by Coordination cost as layers multiply latency and tokens on every decision.'), ('Safety researcher', 'Layering cannot create authority, so humans must remain the approval ceiling. The protection that carries weight is reserving irreversible and high-value approvals to humans, enforcing the authority matrix in runtime rather than prompt text, and capping delegation depth. The operator should verify runtime denies mid-level self-approval, review supervisor-workers and dual-control linkages, and confirm escalation actually reaches a human.')], 'handoff-swarm': [('Evaluation methodologist', 'Agent Handoff or Swarm lets peers transfer conversation and task state to the best-fit agent through a Handoff tool, State transfer protocol, and Registry, with any agent able to route back and terminal agents escalating to humans. That helps support and general triage stay flexible. Yet its documented failure modes interact, with Context loss on handoff dropping constraints, Handoff loops ping-ponging tasks, and Privilege escalation via handoff steering toward a permissive agent.'), ('Safety researcher', 'Flexibility needs a narrow corridor, otherwise routing becomes the exploit. The protections that carry weight are structured handoff payloads with mandatory constraints, budget, and risk fields, a handoff count cap leading to auto-human transfer, and allowlist-only target selection. The operator should verify payload completeness, monitor loop counts, and audit specialist-triage and group-chat-moderator linkages for permissive targets.')], 'blackboard': [('Memory-systems researcher', 'Blackboard coordinates specialist agents through a shared Blackboard with typed sections rather than direct messaging, with a Monitor or controller merging contributions and resolving conflicts. That helps engineering, research, and healthcare combine expertise without tangled channels. The tension is shared-state fragility, with Board vandalism where one compromised agent overwrites others and Race conditions where concurrent writes produce incoherent state that later readers treat as settled.'), ('Evaluation methodologist', 'Shared writing needs versioned control, not goodwill. The protections that carry weight are append-only sections with per-agent ACLs where edits become diffs requiring monitor merge, optimistic concurrency control, and full provenance on every contribution. The operator should verify ACL enforcement, check conflict resolution logs, and audit supervisor-workers and audit-trail linkages to confirm overwritten work is detectable and recoverable.')], 'debate-council': [('Evaluation methodologist', 'Multi-Agent Debate convenes debater agents with a Judge and Round controller to answer independently, exchange rebuttals, and converge through judging or human synthesis, surfacing disagreement before production for finance, legal, and strategy. That independence helps catch blind spots. Yet its documented failure modes warn of Groupthink converging early on the majority wrong answer, Cost and latency scaling with debater count, and an Injected debater steering the council from poisoned context.'), ('Safety researcher', 'Independence must be staged, not assumed. The protections that carry weight are a blind first round without cross-visibility to prevent anchoring, a judge requirement to document why dissent was rejected, and per-debater budgets. The operator should verify rebuttal logs preserve dissent, check self-consistency and skeptical-reasoning and ensemble-verify linkages, and confirm injected content cannot silently set the verdict.')], 'consensus-voting': [('Evaluation methodologist', 'Consensus Voting applies formal quorum, weighted votes, and veto rights through a Voting registry and Tally engine, requiring k-of-n approval for risky actions with ties and vetoes escalating to humans. That helps finance and governance make agent decisions explicit. The tension is vote integrity, with Sybil agents spawned to outvote safeguards and Vote buying via context where shared context anchors all voters toward the same flawed rationale.'), ('Safety researcher', 'Rules help only if identities and contexts stay distinct. The protections that carry weight are binding votes to distinct registered identities with distinct contexts, keeping human veto always available and logged, and including at least one adversarially prompted checker in quorum. The operator should verify identity binding, test debate-council and dual-control escalation paths, and confirm no shared prompt silently aligns the electorate.')], 'specialist-triage': [('Continual-learning researcher', 'Front-Desk Triage uses a cheap intake agent to classify intent and risk through a Triage agent, Specialist pool, and Escalation ladder, routing to specialists while retaining escalation authority. That helps support, healthcare, and legal move fast on routine work. The tension is Triage under-classification, where an emergency is rated routine and human response is delayed because the intake underestimated risk and the specialist never re-escalates in time.'), ('Safety researcher', 'Speed cannot come at the cost of missing the emergency. The protections that carry weight are over-triage bias for safety-critical domains to fail safe and a mandatory human route for self-harm, violence, and legal triggers. The operator should verify trigger coverage, audit routing and handoff-swarm handoffs for downgrades, and confirm specialists can return cases to triage with notes intact.')], 'sequential-pipeline': [('Evaluation methodologist', 'Sequential Handoff Pipeline orders specialist Stage agents with Stage gates to transform an artifact through fixed stages, each passing or failing with rationale and looping back to its producer on failure. That helps content, engineering, and legal keep draft, fact-check, and review responsibilities separate. The tension is Gate capture by upstream style, where later stages defer to an earlier confident tone instead of applying independent scrutiny and defects flow through polished prose.'), ('Safety researcher', 'Order helps only if each gate judges alone. The protections that carry weight are independent contexts per stage and gates with explicit machine-checkable criteria. The operator should verify stage contexts do not leak confidence across steps, check gate logs for prompt-chaining and evaluator-optimizer rigor, and confirm failures actually loop back rather than being waved through.')], 'auction-allocation': [('Continual-learning researcher', 'Market Allocation has workers bid on tasks with cost, time, and confidence estimates through a Bid registry, Allocator, and Performance auditor that assigns work to maximize a global objective and recalibrates chronic over-bidders. That helps logistics and operations match tasks to capacity. The tension pairs Bid collusion converging on inflated bids with Over-promising where optimistic confidence wins bids then fails, so allocation rewards confident misestimation over honest capability.'), ('Evaluation methodologist', 'Bidding needs scoring after the fact, not just before. The protections that carry weight are post-hoc calibration scoring of bid accuracy and caps on allocation share per agent. The operator should verify calibration histories, check concentration under supervisor-workers patterns, and confirm over-promisers lose share rather than accumulating ever more critical tasks on inflated promises.')], 'group-chat-moderator': [('Evaluation methodologist', 'Group Chat with Moderator hosts open speakers under a Moderator and Turn controller that grants the floor, prevents loops, and summarizes for general and strategy work. That openness helps diverse views surface. The tension is control capture, with Moderator capture where injected content manipulates who speaks and Runaway discussion where endless rounds produce cost without decision. Once floor control is steered, the summary inherits the attacker framing.'), ('Safety researcher', 'Openness needs a pinned chair. The protections that carry weight are turn and round caps with a pinned moderator prompt, logged moderator decisions, and escalation on deadlock. The operator should verify caps actually close discussions, review logs for debate-council and handoff-swarm manipulation, and confirm the moderator cannot be re-instructed by speaker content mid-thread.')], 'red-team-pair': [('Safety researcher', 'Red Team and Blue Team pairs a Red agent against a Blue defender through an Attack taxonomy and Verdict log, iterating attacks and patches until the taxonomy is exhausted or budget caps stop the rounds. That helps cybersecurity and general hardening before release. The tension is Collusive red team effort where red raises only shallow objections, so blue patches trivia and the artifact ships with its real weaknesses untested and logged as reviewed.'), ('Evaluation methodologist', 'Adversarial value comes from coverage, not rounds. The protections that carry weight are requiring red to cover a mandated threat taxonomy with a coverage report and enforcing a budget cap on rounds. The operator should verify taxonomy coverage in the verdict log, check skeptical-reasoning and eval-harness linkages, and confirm shallow passes cannot satisfy the gate.')], 'shadow-agents': [('Evaluation methodologist', 'Shadow Agents run a silent twin alongside production through a Shadow runtime and Differ, receiving the same inputs, comparing parallel decisions, and promoting only after parity for devops, finance, and general changes. That helps catch prompt and model regressions before trust shifts. The tension is Shadow divergence ignored, where diff alerts accumulate without triage and production keeps running while evidence of mismatch piles up unreviewed.'), ('Safety researcher', 'Parity without ownership is theater. The protections that carry weight are a divergence SLO with a named owner and burn-down plus sandbox enforcement guaranteeing the shadow has no side effects. The operator should verify alert triage timeliness, confirm sandbox isolation, and audit canary-shadow and dry-run-tools promotion criteria so divergence blocks promotion rather than merely logging it.')], 'function-calling': [('Memory-systems researcher', 'Structured Function Calling constrains tool use with a Schema registry, Validator, and Result normalizer, describing tools with strict schemas, validating syntax and semantics at runtime, and returning results verbatim without reinterpretation. That mechanical backbone helps general actions stay typed. The tension pairs Schema-bypass via free text carrying injection in unvalidated strings with Result re-interpretation where the model reads tool error strings as instructions to obey.'), ('Safety researcher', 'Typing must extend into meaning and presentation. The protections that carry weight are semantic validation beyond JSON Schema with allowlists, ranges, and cross-field rules, rendering tool results as quoted data with delimiters, and rejecting unknown fields. The operator should verify validators against tool-use and structured-output expectations and confirm error text cannot become instructions.')], 'tool-retrieval': [('Memory-systems researcher', 'Dynamic Tool Retrieval indexes tool descriptions and retrieves the top-k schemas per task through a Tool index, Retriever, and Allowlist filter instead of exposing hundreds of tools at once. That helps general and enterprise agents stay focused and within context. The tension is Tool smuggling, where a malicious third-party tool ranks into context and gets invoked because relevance outranked trust and the model treats retrieved availability as permission.'), ('Safety researcher', 'Relevance cannot outrank permission. The protections that carry weight are scoping retrieval by caller permission before relevance ranking and requiring human vetting plus sandbox-only tier for new or low-reputation tools. The operator should verify permission filters run first, audit registry and tool-use bindings, and confirm unvetted tools cannot reach production context through ranking tricks.')], 'code-as-action': [('Continual-learning researcher', 'Code-as-Action has the agent write and execute code against a tool SDK through a Code generator, Sandbox runtime, and Result parser, capturing stdout and artifacts instead of chaining many tool calls. That helps engineering, data, and devops express complex logic compactly. Yet its critical failure modes compound, with Sandbox escape to host or secrets, Destructive code harming shared volumes or production tables, and Exfiltration shipping secrets out through allowed egress.'), ('Safety researcher', 'Capability here demands default denial. The protections that carry weight are micro-VM or container sandboxing with no network by default, egress allowlists, read-only filesystems with tmpfs, short-lived scoped tokens instead of production credentials, and pre-execution scans plus artifact review. The operator should verify sandbox-execution, computer-use, and data-loss-prevention controls and confirm generated code cannot reach standing secrets.')], 'computer-use': [('Evaluation methodologist', 'Computer Use operates a real UI from screenshots with click and typing actions through a Screen capturer, Action executor, and End-state verifier when no API exists, looping until the intended end state holds. That helps operations and general legacy workflows. Yet its documented failure modes are severe, with Clicking the wrong window on stale screens, Visible injected instructions rendered on the page, and Credential exposure where typed passwords and recordings leak secrets.'), ('Safety researcher', 'Pixels are untrusted input, so verification must target outcomes not clicks. The protections that carry weight are verifying end state rather than clicks while treating page text as untrusted, isolating OS sessions with passwords withheld from screenshots, and still requiring underlying approval gates for financial actions. The operator should verify browser-agent and input-sanitization handling and confirm GUI convenience never bypasses authorization.')], 'browser-agent': [('Safety researcher', 'Browser Research Agent navigates, extracts, and summarizes the web through a Browser driver, Content extractor, Injection shield, and Citation tracker, facing the largest prompt-injection surface agents have for research, general, and procurement. The tension spans Hidden-text injection with white-on-white or comment instructions, Paywall and ToS violations ignoring access rules, and Malicious payload download where fetched hostile files are opened and honored.'), ('Evaluation methodologist', 'Breadth needs a narrow data channel. The protections that carry weight are stripping scripts, styles, and hidden text into a delimited data channel, enforcing an egress allowlist with no credentials in the browser profile, and filtering outputs derived from web content. The operator should verify hidden text never reaches instructions, audit input-sanitization and code-as-action boundaries, and confirm citations survive extraction intact.')], 'sandbox-execution': [('Safety researcher', 'Sandboxed Execution runs every untrusted computation in a disposable capability-limited environment through a Sandbox manager, seccomp and AppArmor and egress policy, and a Log shipper, with per-task microVMs, CPU and memory and time limits, and destruction after the task. That helps engineering, devops, and general isolation. Yet its documented failure modes warn of Misconfigured egress with broad wildcards, Shared sandbox reuse leaking state and secrets, and Kernel escape through container flaws.'), ('Evaluation methodologist', 'Disposability must be literal and default-deny. The protections that carry weight are default-deny egress with explicit per-task hostname allowlists, fresh sandboxes per task with no reuse, and microVM-class isolation with seccomp profiles for hostile code. The operator should verify allowlists against code-as-action needs, audit egress-control and data-loss-prevention logs, and confirm retained audit logs cannot reintroduce secrets.')], 'simulation-twin': [('Continual-learning researcher', 'Simulation or Digital Twin rehearses plans against a simulated environment copy through a Simulator, Constraint checker, and Promotion gate, loading current state, scoring outcomes, and promoting only plans passing safety constraints. That helps robotics, logistics, finance, and energy test before touching reality. The tension is Sim-to-real gap, where the twin omits the very failure mode that occurs in reality and a passing simulation confers false confidence on an unsafe plan.'), ('Safety researcher', 'Simulation should inform, never authorize. The protections that carry weight are maintaining a failure-mode library the twin must reproduce and keeping simulation advisory while real-world guardrails stay enforced. The operator should verify library coverage, check dry-run-tools and canary-shadow promotion evidence, and confirm no plan reaches reality on simulated approval alone without independent checks.')], 'dry-run-tools': [('Evaluation methodologist', 'Dry-Run Diff Mode gives state-changing tools a would-be diff path through dry-run capable tools, a Diff visualizer, and Confirm flow, returning simulated receipts until a confirmed call applies with an idempotency key. That helps devops, finance, and procurement preview impact. The tension pairs Dry-run lies where hidden webhooks diverge from the preview with Mode confusion where the agent believes it previews while actually applying for real.'), ('Safety researcher', 'Preview value depends on server truth. The protections that carry weight are server-enforced mode included in signed responses, enumerating secondary effects like notifications and webhooks in the diff, and logging dry-run receipts to the audit trail. The operator should verify mode flags against checkpoint-rollback and approval-gates, and confirm the diff reliably predicts the real apply before confirmation.')], 'mcp-registry': [('Memory-systems researcher', 'Tool Registry in MCP style centralizes tools through a Registry, Binding policy, Reputation scoring, and Audit, registering owner, scope, and data class, restricting which agents may bind which tools, and versioning schemas with change review. That helps enterprise and general governance. Yet its documented failure modes escalate, with Tool poisoning rewriting descriptions into instructions, Rug-pull update swapping trusted tools after vetting, and Shadow tools binding directly to unvetted endpoints.'), ('Safety researcher', 'Centralization must pin trust, not just list it. The protections that carry weight are pinning tool schema hashes with re-vetting on change, serving descriptions from the registry rather than the live server, and binding policy limiting which agent and task classes may use which tiers. The operator should verify hash pins, audit tool-retrieval and least-privilege bindings, and confirm direct endpoint bypass is denied.')], 'skill-library': [('Continual-learning researcher', 'Skill Library packages versioned tested skills of prompts, tools, and tests through a Skill registry, Test harness, and Loader, letting agents load capabilities by match while tests gate updates for enterprise and engineering. That reuse beats ad-hoc prompting. The tension is Skill with hidden tool calls, where a community skill quietly contains exfiltration steps that execute under the agent authority once loaded and trusted as a reviewed capability.'), ('Safety researcher', 'Reuse needs permission transparency before execution. The protections that carry weight are reviewing and statically scanning skills for tool calls with required permissions declared up front plus permission diff review on updates. The operator should verify declared versus actual calls, audit registry and eval-harness coverage, and confirm version bumps cannot silently widen tool access without approval.')], 'tool-sandbox': [('Evaluation methodologist', 'Tool Dry-Run Tier ships every state-changing tool with a read-only simulation variant through a Tool manifest, Tier manager, and Simulator, starting agents in simulate-only tier and promoting to apply tier only after eval pass and review. That helps general and devops onboarding stay safe. The tension is Simulate and apply divergence, where the two implementations drift so evaluated behavior no longer predicts real effects and promotion certifies the wrong artifact.'), ('Safety researcher', 'Tiers hold only if parity is proven and promotion is external. The protections that carry weight are generating both variants from one spec with contract tests enforcing parity and runtime-enforced tiers where agents cannot self-promote. The operator should verify contract tests against dry-run-tools and sandbox-execution expectations and confirm promotion requires independent eval and human review.')], 'coding-agent-pipeline': [('Continual-learning researcher', 'Coding Agent Pipeline moves spec to plan to sandboxed implementation to tests to second-agent review to human merge through a Planner, Sandboxed implementer, Test runner, Reviewer agent, and Merge gate, with code never merged by its author. That helps engineering keep velocity with separation. Yet its documented failure modes warn of Destructive migrations, Test gaming weakening tests, Secret leakage in diffs, and Dependency confusion installing typosquatted packages.'), ('Safety researcher', 'Separation must reach infrastructure, not just roles. The protections that carry weight are mandatory migration review with snapshots and rollback while production databases stay unreachable, reviewed test diffs with mutation testing, pre-commit secret scans with allowlisted pinned dependencies, and deployment through human approval gates. The operator should verify code-as-action and sandbox-execution and approval-gates enforcement end to end.')], 'support-triage': [('Evaluation methodologist', 'Customer Support Playbook classifies intent and risk through Triage, a RAG resolver, Policy-gated actions, and Escalation, resolving low-risk work from cited sources while bounding money, PII, and legal actions and escalating with transcript summaries. That helps support stay fast yet contained. The tension pairs Social-engineered refunds repeatedly extracting credits with PII echo restating full card numbers to the wrong recipient after a plausible complaint.'), ('Safety researcher', 'Helpfulness cannot override account and data boundaries. The protections that carry weight are refund caps with per-customer velocity limits aggregated across channels, never echoing PII with vault-based re-identification and redacted transcripts, and verifying account ownership before any account action. The operator should verify routing and budget-guardrails and content-shielding enforcement and confirm escalation preserves provenance without leaking secrets.')], 'trading-agent': [('Safety researcher', 'Trading Playbook separates proposing from disposing through a Signal agent, Risk engine, Executor, and Kill switch, with citation-checked signals, validated sizing and exposure, broker execution under hard caps, and human desk oversight for finance. That structure helps speed stay bounded. Yet its documented failure modes warn of Runaway loop ordering duplicating orders, Stale-signal trading on frozen feeds, and Strategy drift via memory rewriting the mandate mid-session.'), ('Evaluation methodologist', 'Autonomy here must sit beneath broker truth. The protections that carry weight are hard position and order-rate caps outside the agent runtime, staleness gates defaulting flat, immutable strategy mandates changeable only under dual control, and a daily-tested kill switch. The operator should verify budget-guardrails and circuit-breaker and idempotency-keys linkages and confirm retries cannot multiply orders.')], 'healthcare-triage': [('Safety researcher', 'Clinical Triage is decision support only through Intake, Guideline RAG, Escalation engine, and PHI vault, using minimal tokenized context, guideline-grounded cited suggestions, immediate escalation on red flags, and full audit for governance. That helps healthcare stay assistive. The tension is severe, with Autonomous clinical action suggesting unsupervised dosage from hallucinated interactions and PHI to third-party model exposure when un-minimized context leaves approved boundaries.'), ('Evaluation methodologist', 'Support value depends on hard clinical boundaries. The protections that carry weight are a hard policy requiring licensed human sign-off for clinical action, PHI tokenization before external calls to approved endpoints only, and deterministic dosage calculators rather than LLM outputs. The operator should verify PII filtering and human-in-the-loop and retrieval-grounded enforcement and confirm no dosage or diagnosis ships without review.')], 'sre-agent': [('Continual-learning researcher', 'SRE Playbook diagnoses freely but remediates narrowly through a Diagnostic reader, Remediation planner, Change gate, and Rollback manager, granting broad read access while ranking remediations by blast radius and auto-remediating only pre-approved low-risk actions. That helps devops learn quickly without granting write freedom. The tension pairs Over-broad fix restarting the wrong stateful service into cascade with Runaway scaling triggering cost explosion from well-meant automation.'), ('Safety researcher', 'Read freedom must not imply write freedom. The protections that carry weight are a per-service remediation allowlist with human gating for stateful systems, spend-per-hour caps on infra actions, and change windows with auto-rollback. The operator should verify self-healing and budget-guardrails and checkpoint-rollback linkages and confirm every change stays reversible or explicitly approved.')], 'research-citation-agent': [('Evaluation methodologist', 'Research Agent with Citation Enforcement collects through browser and RAG with provenance, drafts claims citing source IDs, and passes a verifier that resolves each citation and checks entailment through a Collector, Claim writer, Citation verifier, and Report renderer for research and legal. That helps block fabrication before human decisions. The tension pairs Fabricated citations inventing confident papers with Source laundering elevating low-quality SEO content into apparent authority.'), ('Safety researcher', 'Collection is easy, verification is the gate. The protections that carry weight are requiring citations to resolve to retrieved content hashes with entailment checks, surfacing source-quality tiers from primary to SEO content, and enforcing abstain over fabricate at the verifier. The operator should verify browser-agent and provenance-citation and retrieval-grounded linkages and confirm unverifiable claims are dropped, not softened.')], 'procurement-agent': [('Safety researcher', 'Procurement Playbook lets the agent search, compare, and draft orders through Intake, Research agent, PO drafter, Spend guard, Approval workflow, and Processor caps, with budgets from requester and policy, provenance on claims, and dual-control approval above threshold for procurement and finance. Its documented failure modes warn of Prompt-injected purchase moving large sums in minutes, Vendor spoofing to lookalike names, and Threshold splitting evading review with small orders.'), ('Evaluation methodologist', 'I agree the spend guard must sit outside persuasion. The protections that carry weight are deterministic middleware the model cannot bypass or self-approve, vendor identity checks with cooling off for first-time vendors, rolling aggregate caps with processor-level enforcement, and hashed audited provenance per order. The operator should verify budget-guardrails and dual-control and approval-gates and browser-agent handling on every purchase path.')], 'least-privilege': [('Safety researcher', 'Least Privilege Scoping gives the agent only the minimum credentials and data access the current task needs, with per-task capability sets and short-lived scoped tokens minted from policy, and denial by default. I read its value against standing broad credentials where one injected prompt means full breach, plus scope creep over time and token relay to untrusted tools. The counter is per-task per-tool tokens with short TTL, review and revocation of unused grants, and audience-bound tokens, close to policy engine and agent identity work.'), ('Evaluation methodologist', 'What convinces me here is that the control is structural rather than rhetorical, since elevation is logged and access denied by default. I would sharpen the claim though: short-lived tokens only help if scope creep is actually pruned, because permissions added for edge cases tend to persist. The record answers that with periodic permission diff review and automatic revocation, plus audience binding to specific tool endpoints, which keeps finance, devops, healthcare and general deployments honest.')], 'policy-engine': [('Safety researcher', 'The Policy Engine moves rules out of the prompt and into deterministic runtime middleware, expressing each action as actor, action, resource and context, then returning allow, deny or require-approval with a decision log. Its named failures are prompt-only guardrails that vanish under injection or truncation, policy bypass through a new tool path, and default-allow drift. The defense is enforcement at the tool layer independent of the model, default-deny with new action classes starting at require-approval, and versioned policy with a test suite.'), ('Continual-learning researcher', 'I agree the decisive move is independence from the model, since anything the model can rewrite is not a guardrail. My caution is that rules silently gap as actions evolve, which is exactly the default-allow drift failure the record names. Versioning plus decision logging and a policy change test suite address that, and the ties to least privilege, approval gates and budget guardrails show where this engine sits for finance, healthcare, devops and general agents.')], 'budget-guardrails': [('Safety researcher', 'Financial Guardrails put dollar-denominated limits around the agent, with per-task spend caps set by requester and policy, screening on amount, vendor, category, velocity and baseline deviation, and a hard stop with human approval above threshold or on anomaly. The failures are single-approver automation where the agent approves its own spend, splitting under thresholds, card details sitting in prompt context, and new-vendor rush under urgent framing. Dual control with an independent policy engine, rolling aggregate caps, processor-level hard caps and vendor allowlists with cooling-off answer each one.'), ('Memory-systems researcher', 'The subtle point is memory of spend, since splitting only works when each charge forgets the last. I like that the record answers with a spend ledger plus velocity and aggregate caps over rolling windows, so many small charges still trip the guard. Keeping the card out of model context with tokens and processor-level caps mirroring software limits is the other load-bearing choice, and urgency framing treated as a risk signal rather than a bypass closes the new-vendor rush.')], 'quota-rate-limit': [('Evaluation methodologist', 'Quotas and Rate Limiting cap volume and rate per agent, tool, tenant and action class, using sliding-window counters with burst and sustained limits that slow down or block with an alert on breach. The record warns of limits keyed too coarsely so one noisy tenant starves others, and bypass via sub-agents that arrive with fresh quotas. The protections are a quota hierarchy where children share the parent budget, stricter per-action-class quotas for outward-facing actions, and alerts at partial burn with blocking at full burn.'), ('Safety researcher', 'I would defend this as the blast-radius limiter of last resort, but only with the hierarchy intact. Without children sharing the parent budget, every fan-out becomes a fresh allowance and the ceiling is decorative. The record gets this right by tying the pattern to budget-bounded execution and financial guardrails, so rate limits, spend caps and loop bounds reinforce rather than duplicate each other across general and finance workloads.')], 'approval-gates': [('Safety researcher', 'Approval Gates require explicit human approval with full context before irreversible or high-impact actions execute, built from an action classifier, an approval service and an evidence pack describing what, why, sources, diff and risk, with expiry on approvals. Failures include gate bypass via abstraction where a different tool reaches the same effect, evidence pack manipulation by injected content, and approval fatigue. The record enforces gates at the effect layer keyed on effect rather than tool name, with provenance chains, raw diffs, highlighted untrusted content, sampling audits and fatigue metrics.'), ('Continual-learning researcher', 'My dissent is mild: evidence packs improve decisions only if reviewers can actually see the poison. I agree with the record that showing the provenance chain and flagging injected content matters more than pack length. Auto-tuning thresholds from fatigue metrics is the continual-learning hook here, since gate strictness should adapt as rubber-stamping rises, and the links to human-in-the-loop, dual control and reversibility-first design keep the gate inside a larger human process.')], 'dual-control': [('Safety researcher', 'Dual Control requires two independent approvers for high-risk actions, where neither approver may be the acting agent, using an approver registry with tally, expiry and full audit. Its failures are approval rings where automated agents approve each other, and one human with two tabs producing formal but not real dual control. Protections bind approver identity to distinct humans or a human plus policy engine with authentication, bar agents categorically from approving, and review approval graphs periodically for collusion patterns, alongside approval gates and voting protocols.'), ('Evaluation methodologist', 'I find the four-eyes framing persuasive precisely because it names its own defeat modes. Approval rings are the case I would test first, since agent approvers can look independent while sharing context. The record answers with distinct identities and contexts plus authentication, and the periodic review of approval graphs gives an evaluator something observable to check in finance and devops deployments rather than a promise of independence.')], 'input-sanitization': [('Safety researcher', 'Input Sanitization screens everything entering context, including user input, tool output, retrieved documents and web pages, detecting instruction overrides, hidden text, encoded payloads and exfiltration instructions, then stripping, delimiting as inert data, quarantining or blocking with human review. Failures are pattern-list myopia against novel or encoded phrasings, over-blocking of legitimate discussion, and injection inside tool output while teams watch only user input. The defense assumes all external content is hostile, separates data from instructions, and keeps an attack corpus with block-rate drift monitoring.'), ('Memory-systems researcher', 'The memory angle matters because a single quarantined passage that still gets stored becomes a standing instruction. I agree with treating untrusted content as data wrapped in delimiters and never concatenated as instructions. Defense in depth is the honest part of this record: the shield plus least privilege plus approval gates, rather than the shield alone, with ties to browser agents, content shielding and RAG poisoning defense carrying the web and retrieval vectors.')], 'content-shielding': [('Safety researcher', 'Output and Content Shielding screens agent outputs before they leave the system for personal data, secrets, toxic or brand-damaging content and compliance violations, using a classifier with redact, rewrite or block paths plus logging of redactions for tuning. Failures are evasion via encoding with personal data split across fields or turns, and over-reliance where upstream leaks are excused because the shield will catch them. Protections call for session-level rather than message-level scanning, upstream minimization so sensitive data never enters context, and a redaction feedback loop into prompt tuning.'), ('Evaluation methodologist', 'I would sharpen the measurement point: per-message pass rates can look clean while a session leaks across turns, which is why session-level scanning is the load-bearing protection here. Upstream minimization is the evaluator-friendly claim too, since preventing sensitive data from entering context is observable in a way that output rewriting is not. The links to data loss prevention and PII redaction show this shield as one layer rather than the whole story.')], 'output-filtering-pii': [('Memory-systems researcher', 'PII Detection and Redaction works at ingress, inside context and at egress, combining pattern detectors with entity recognition, masking or tokenizing before the model call, and re-identifying only inside approved downstream systems through a vault. Detector gaps on free-text personal data and the vault becoming a concentrated honeypot are the named failures. Layered pattern plus model detection with per-domain dictionaries, vault hardening with encryption, access audit and split knowledge, and egress scanning as a final line form the recorded defense across healthcare, support, finance and legal settings.'), ('Safety researcher', 'I agree with the vault caution most: centralizing personal data to protect it creates exactly the store an attacker wants. Encryption, auditing and split knowledge are therefore not optional extras in this record. The other point I would stress is re-identification discipline, since masking before the call only holds if only approved systems can reverse it, with content shielding and data loss prevention sitting alongside as companion layers.')], 'provenance-citation': [('Evaluation methodologist', 'Provenance and Citation Enforcement requires every claim and action to carry a verifiable chain of which input, tool and policy version produced it, with source tags on context items, cited source identifiers per claim, and a verifier checking support before action. The named failure is decorative citations that look real but do not support the claim. The protections resolve each citation and check entailment rather than existence, and block actions with incomplete provenance instead of warning, which makes this pattern testable rather than stylistic across legal, research, finance and healthcare work.'), ('Safety researcher', 'Blocking rather than warning is the decision I would defend, since warnings on missing provenance degrade into click-through under pressure. The chain-of-custody log plus citation verifier gives reviewers something concrete to audit, and the ties to audit trails and retrieval-grounded answering place provenance at the boundary between evidence and action, where it can actually stop an unsupported move.')], 'audit-trail': [('Safety researcher', 'The Immutable Audit Trail keeps an append-only tamper-evident log of every prompt, tool call, policy decision, approval and outcome, with structured events per loop iteration, hash-chained or write-once storage, and replay tooling for postmortems and eval datasets. Failures are logging the secrets themselves into the store, partial trails where sub-agent actions go unlogged, and log viewers that re-execute hostile content. Protections redact or tokenize at write time with hashes and pointers for large payloads, mandate logging in the runtime rather than per agent, and treat viewed logs as untrusted data.'), ('Evaluation methodologist', 'What makes this evaluable is replay: structured events plus hash chaining turn an incident into a reconstructable sequence rather than a narrative. I would stress mandatory runtime logging, since opt-in per-agent logging guarantees the partial-trail failure the record names. Redaction at write time is the right tension to hold, keeping forensic value while avoiding a personal-data store, with provenance and structured event logging as natural companions.')], 'circuit-breaker': [('Safety researcher', 'The Circuit Breaker trips automatically on anomaly across looping, error rate, spend and output class, freezing the agent, checkpointing state and alerting, with half-open probes and manual reset after review plus a human-operable global kill switch. Failures are the breaker owned by the agent that resets itself, false-trip fatigue that gets the breaker disabled, and trips without containment where in-flight side effects continue. Protections keep breaker state in the runtime only, pair trips with containment that cancels calls and revokes tokens, and tune thresholds on shadow data while watching false-trip rates.'), ('Continual-learning researcher', 'My addition is that tuning is continual work, not a one-time threshold. Thresholds learned on shadow data and reviewed against false-trip rates let the breaker adapt as agent behavior shifts. Containment is the part I would refuse to soften: stopping the loop while payments or tool calls already in flight still land is not containment, so cancelling calls and revoking tokens on trip, with ties to bounded execution and incident playbooks, carries the pattern.')], 'structured-output': [('Evaluation methodologist', 'Structured Output forces actions and answers into schemas through constrained decoding or strict validation, with grammar or schema-constrained generation, rejection of non-conforming outputs, and free text confined to designated fields. The named failure is schema without semantics, where valid JSON carries absurd values. The recorded answer is semantic validation with ranges, allowlists and cross-field rules, plus rejection rather than repair where possible, which keeps malformed or smuggled instructions from sliding through on syntactic correctness alone.'), ('Safety researcher', 'I agree that rejection beats repair for high-stakes actions, since repairing a hostile payload risks preserving its intent. Constrained decoding plus a validator narrows the side channel that free-form text provides, and the links to function calling and validation loops show where structure meets execution: schemas at generation time, executable checks before acceptance, which together leave less room for free-text smuggling.')], 'eval-harness-redteam': [('Evaluation methodologist', 'The Eval Harness runs a versioned regression suite of safety and capability evals on every prompt, model or policy change before deploy, built from benign and attack prompts with expected policy outcomes, blocking regressions and folding real incidents back into the set. The failure is eval overfitting, where prompts are tuned to the known corpus and novel attacks pass. Hold-out attack sets with rotating external red teams plus turning production incidents into eval cases quickly are the recorded protections, with red-team pairs, canary rollout and drift monitoring as companions.'), ('Safety researcher', 'Folding incidents back into the corpus is the practice I would insist on, since a harness that never learns from production is a snapshot. Hold-out sets matter for the same reason: they test generalization rather than memorization of the known attacks. Gating deployment in CI makes the harness a control rather than commentary, which is what lets it catch prompt or policy regressions before they reach general deployment.')], 'canary-shadow': [('Safety researcher', 'Canary and Shadow Deployment ramps new agent behaviors gradually from shadow with no side effects to a small canary with full guardrails, then staged rollout with auto-rollback on service-objective breach, using a traffic splitter, objective monitor and rollback automation. The failure is canary without containment, where a small percentage still means a large absolute volume of harmful actions. Protections start the canary on read-only tasks, cap absolute canary side-effect volume rather than percentage alone, and rehearse automatic rollback, with shadow agents and red-team evals alongside.'), ('Evaluation methodologist', 'The absolute-cap point deserves emphasis: percentages hide scale, so a small share of a large system can still cause wide harm. Read-only first exposure plus automatic rehearsed rollback makes the ramp falsifiable, since breach behavior is defined before rollout. Shadow comparison before any live traffic gives a baseline, which is why I read this pattern as measurement discipline applied to deployment across general and devops settings.')], 'drift-monitoring': [('Evaluation methodologist', 'Behavior and Drift Monitoring watches distributions of routes, spend, tool mix, block rates and refusal rates against per-agent baselines, comparing continuously and alerting on significant deviation for investigation. The failure is alert fatigue with no owner, where drift alerts go unwatched. Named protections assign owners and service objectives to drift alerts and link alerts to automatic containment such as rate reduction pending review, with circuit breakers and audit trails as the response path across general and finance deployments.'), ('Continual-learning researcher', 'I see drift monitoring as the continual-learning conscience of the catalog: baselines must be relearned as legitimate behavior shifts, or every product change becomes an anomaly. Owner plus objective plus automatic containment is the right trio, since it pairs detection with a bounded response while a human investigates. Statistical comparison against stored baselines keeps this empirical rather than impressionistic, which is what makes slow behavioral change visible.')], 'incident-playbook': [('Safety researcher', 'The Incident Response Playbook pre-rehearses containment, revocation, blast-radius assessment, notification, recovery and learning, starting the runbook with kill switch and token revocation, querying blast radius from the audit trail, and ending with postmortem-driven eval and policy fixes. The failure is a novel incident with no runbook, forcing improvisation during active harm. Protections are quarterly tabletop exercises with agent-specific scenarios and automated containment playbooks tested like production code, tied to circuit breakers and audit trails across general and devops operations.'), ('Evaluation methodologist', 'Tested like production code is the phrase I would hold onto, since an untested runbook is only a document. Tabletops surface the missing blast-radius tooling before an incident does, and converting postmortems into eval cases plus policy fixes closes the loop back into the harness. Blast-radius queries grounded in the audit trail make scope assessment reconstructable rather than guessed, which is what lets notification and recovery proceed with confidence.')], 'dlp': [('Safety researcher', 'Data Loss Prevention controls what may cross system boundaries through data classification at source, policy over data-class to destination-class pairs, and scanning of outbound payloads with block and alert, using classifiers, an egress proxy and secret scanners. Failures are steganographic exfiltration with secrets encoded into innocuous fields, and new-destination trust where the agent registers an unreviewed webhook. Protections default-deny destinations with review for new endpoints, add entropy and encoding detectors beside pattern matching, and plant canary secrets in context to detect leakage early across enterprise, healthcare and finance boundaries.'), ('Memory-systems researcher', 'Classification at source is the memory-relevant move, since boundary controls fail when they first meet sensitive data at the exit. Canary secrets give the system a tripwire: leaked markers reveal a path before real data follows. Default-deny on destinations keeps the burden of proof on the new endpoint, and the ties to egress control, sandboxed execution and PII filtering show boundary defense as a stack rather than a single scanner.')], 'egress-control': [('Safety researcher', 'Network Egress Control lets agent runtimes reach only explicitly allowlisted endpoints, with per-task egress policy from the tool manifest, proxy enforcement on hostname and indication, and blocked attempts logged as incidents. Failures are allowlist creep through broad wildcards and DNS tunneling where exfiltration moves over DNS while HTTP is filtered. Protections require exact-hostname allowlists with no wildcards plus DNS filtering and logging with blocking of encrypted DNS bypass, supported by sandboxing and data loss prevention across devops and engineering runtimes.'), ('Continual-learning researcher', 'Allowlist creep is the slow failure I would watch, since each convenient wildcard quietly widens the boundary. Exact hostnames plus DNS-layer controls resist that drift, and logging blocked attempts as incidents turns probes into signal. Per-task policy from the tool manifest keeps the boundary scoped to what the current task needs, which connects egress discipline back to least privilege rather than leaving it as pure networking.')], 'irreversible-action-confirm': [('Safety researcher', 'Reversibility-First Design prefers reversible actions and adds confirmation, delay and staged execution where actions are irreversible, using a reversibility classifier, a delay queue and a confirmation flow with end-state verification. The failure is hidden irreversibility, where an outwardly minor action such as sending a message is classified reversible when it is not. Protections maintain an effects-based taxonomy learned from real incidents and default to treating anything external-facing as irreversible, with approval gates, rollback and compensation patterns as companions across finance, devops and general work.'), ('Evaluation methodologist', 'Defaulting external-facing actions to irreversible is the judgment I would endorse, since effects outside the system cannot be recalled by rolling back local state. An effects-based taxonomy maintained from incidents keeps the classifier honest about cases like sent messages or posted content. Queued-with-delay execution adds a cancellation window that pure confirmation lacks, which is why staged execution plus end-state verification earns its place before high-impact moves.')], 'idempotency-keys': [('Evaluation methodologist', 'Idempotency Keys attach a key to every side-effecting call so retries, resumes and replays cannot double-charge or double-deploy, with runtime key generation, server-side deduplication and replay-safe resume after crash or approval. The failure is key reuse across distinct effects, where one key for different intended actions blocks legitimate retries. Protections derive keys from agent, task, action class and arguments with per-effect salt and retain keys beyond the retry window, which keeps finance and devops retries safe alongside interrupt-resume and batch processing patterns.'), ('Safety researcher', 'I read this as the companion that makes retry and resume honest: without server-side deduplication, every retry policy is a double-spend policy. Per-effect salting is the detail that prevents a well-meaning key scheme from merging distinct intentions. Retention beyond the retry window matters equally, since approvals and checkpoints can resume work long after the original attempt, and only a durable dedupe store catches those duplicates.')], 'agent-identity': [('Safety researcher', 'Agent Identity gives every agent a distinct verifiable identity so actions are attributable and requester identity travels with the task, using infrastructure-issued credentials, propagation of end-user identity into downstream authorization, and logging of every action under that identity. Failures are a shared service identity collapsing attribution and authorization, and identity spoofing where the model merely claims to be another agent. Protections hold identity in infrastructure rather than model statements and authorize on the human-plus-agent pair rather than the agent alone, with least privilege and audit trails alongside in enterprise settings.'), ('Memory-systems researcher', 'The infrastructure-held point is decisive for memory too: a stored transcript claiming an identity must never override the credential the runtime holds. Propagating end-user identity downstream prevents the agent from laundering a low-privilege request through its own broader rights. Attribution logging closes the loop, since per-identity action histories make misuse reconstructable, which is what lets least privilege and audit actually refer to someone rather than to the system in general.')], 'uncertainty-abstention': [('Evaluation methodologist', 'Abstention and Graceful Refusal designs refusal as a first-class successful outcome, with defined triggers for low confidence, policy conflict and missing evidence, structured reason codes on abstain, and routing to a staffed human queue. Failures are refusal theater where trivial refusals mask real risk-taking, and abuse of abstention that offloads everything to humans. Protections monitor abstain rates per action class to catch spikes and lulls and keep escalation paths genuinely staffed, with confidence gating and human-in-the-loop as companions across healthcare, finance and legal deployments.'), ('Safety researcher', 'Staffed escalation is what separates real abstention from a decorated error message, since an unstaffed queue turns refusal into a dead end. Per-class abstain-rate monitoring gives both failure modes an observable signature: too little refusal suggests theater, too much suggests offloading. Structured reason codes make those rates analyzable, which is why I would treat abstention telemetry as a safety metric rather than a support statistic.')], 'fan-out-caps': [('Safety researcher', 'Fan-Out and Concurrency Caps set global limits on how many sub-agents or tasks one agent may spawn, using depth and width caps on delegation trees, aggregate budget inheritance where children share the parent quota, and truncation of plans rather than guardrails on breach. The failure is delegation laundering, where an agent delegates to dodge its own limits. Protections enforce caps in the runtime across the whole descendant tree and visualize the delegation graph in the audit trail, tied to orchestrator patterns, rate limiting and bounded execution across general and enterprise hierarchies.'), ('Continual-learning researcher', 'Truncate the plan rather than the guardrails is the line that carries this pattern, since the alternative is negotiating with the ceiling. Runtime enforcement across descendants is what defeats laundering: a child with a fresh budget is not a fresh budget if the meter rolls up. Visualizing delegation in the audit trail makes fan-out legible to reviewers, which matters as hierarchical systems grow beyond what any single prompt can describe.')], 'audit-logging-pattern': [('Evaluation methodologist', 'Structured Event Logging standardizes spans and events for every agent step so traces compose across agents, tools and policies, emitting spans for model calls, tool calls, policy checks and approvals, correlating by task and trace identifiers across sub-agents, and exporting to the observability stack under a retention policy. The failure is personal data inside spans exported to third-party observability vendors. Protections redact at the instrumentation layer and hash large payloads while storing pointers, with immutable audit trails and drift monitoring as consumers of the resulting traces across enterprise and devops estates.'), ('Safety researcher', 'Redaction at instrumentation rather than at export is the safeguard I would keep, since once full prompts leave for a vendor the boundary has already failed. Correlation identifiers are the quiet value here: without shared task and trace identity, sub-agent activity fragments into unrelated events. Standardized spans make cross-agent, cross-tool and cross-policy analysis possible, which is what turns scattered logs into a reconstructable system story.')], 'rag-poison-defense': [('Safety researcher', 'RAG Poisoning Defense protects the retrieval corpus through ingestion scanning for injection patterns, hidden text and provenance, trust tiers per source, anomaly detection on retrieved content with instruction isolation, and corroboration before action. Failures are poisoned SEO content steering purchases or research, poisoned internal documents planted through compromised accounts, and bulk poisoning where many consistent fakes outvote truth. Protections tier retrieval so open-web sources inform but never trigger actions alone, require corroboration across independent trusted sources, review ingestion queues with corpus-shift alerts, and wrap retrieved text as untrusted data.'), ('Memory-systems researcher', 'The corroboration requirement is the memory-systems lesson: a single retrieved passage should never become a standing instruction for action. Trust tiers plus quarantine at retrieval keep untrusted sources informative without letting them drive effects, and corpus-shift alerts catch the bulk-poisoning case where volume simulates consensus. Instruction isolation on retrieved text, with ties to retrieval-grounded answering, input sanitization and vector-memory hygiene, keeps long-lived corpora from becoming long-lived compromises.')], 'confused-deputy-defense': [('Safety researcher', 'Confused-Deputy Defense stops agents with broad authority from acting for low-privilege requesters by capturing end-user identity at intake, propagating on-behalf-of identity through every tool call, and authorizing downstream on the user-plus-agent pair with least privilege winning. The failure is agent-ambient authority, where a junior ticket triggers executive-level data rights. Protections compute effective scope as the intersection of agent and requester rights, require the requester to hold the same right for sensitive reads, and keep delegation tokens short-lived and audience-bound, with agent identity and least privilege alongside.'), ('Evaluation methodologist', 'Intersection rather than union is the formal point worth preserving: effective scope must shrink to what both parties hold, never expand to the stronger. I would test the ambient-authority case directly, since it is the most plausible production surprise. Short-lived audience-bound delegation tokens bound the blast radius in time and place, and authorizing on the pair rather than the agent alone makes the requester visible to every downstream check across enterprise and finance flows.')], 'retry-backoff': [('Evaluation methodologist', 'Retry with Exponential Backoff and Jitter bounds retries on transient failures with growing delays plus randomization, built from an error classifier and a backoff scheduler that escalates terminal errors instead of retrying them. Failures are retrying non-idempotent actions so a payment charges twice, and retry storms where synchronized retries overload the downstream. Protections retry only idempotent calls or calls carrying idempotency keys and hold a global retry budget across agents, with idempotency keys and fallback chains as companions across general and devops operations.'), ('Safety researcher', 'Distinguishing retryable from terminal errors is the safety core here, since retrying a terminal refusal just repeats the harm. Pairing every retried side effect with an idempotency key turns the classifier from advice into enforcement. A global retry budget matters at fleet scale, where per-agent limits still sum to a storm, so jitter plus a shared ceiling keeps transient-error handling from becoming a self-inflicted overload.')], 'fallback-chain': [('Safety researcher', 'The Fallback Chain degrades in order from primary model to smaller model to deterministic heuristic to human, using a tier registry with health-gated selection and logging of which tier served. The failure is an unsafe heuristic tier that skips guardrails in the name of simplicity. Protections place guardrails below all tiers in a shared gateway and give degraded tiers narrower action rights rather than wider ones, with pipeline fallback and graceful degradation alongside, so reduced capability never means reduced oversight in general deployments.'), ('Continual-learning researcher', 'Narrower rights in degraded mode is the insight I would underline: a weaker model should be allowed to do less, not more. Health-gated selection plus logging of the serving tier makes degradation observable, so reviewers can see how often the system runs diminished. Keeping guardrails beneath every tier means fallback changes capability without renegotiating safety, which is what lets ordered degradation stay ordered rather than sliding into an unguarded heuristic.')], 'saga-compensation': [('Safety researcher', 'Saga Compensation handles distributed multi-step transactions by pairing each step with a compensating action, running compensations in reverse on failure, and logging saga state for audit, through an orchestrator and a compensation registry. Failures are missing compensation where steps like sent messages have no undo, and compensation failure cascades where the undo itself fails mid-chain. Protections classify steps without compensation as irreversible with an upfront approval gate, rehearse compensation paths, and alert on partial-saga states, with rollback and reversibility-first design alongside across finance, devops and logistics flows.'), ('Memory-systems researcher', 'Saga state as durable memory is what makes partial completion recoverable rather than mysterious. I agree that steps without undo must be gated before execution, since no runtime cleverness restores a sent message. Rehearsed compensation paths plus alerts on partial states keep the orchestrator honest about the middle of the chain, where most real sagas actually fail, and the audit log of saga state turns recovery into something reviewable.')], 'validation-loop': [('Evaluation methodologist', 'The Validation Loop checks outputs against executable criteria such as tests, schemas and lint before accepting them, generating, running validators, and feeding failures back for bounded regeneration through a validator suite, feedback formatter and bound controller. The failure is validators too weak, where green tests accompany a broken product. Protections review validators like production code and keep them independent from the generator model, with evaluator-optimizer and structured output as companions across engineering and general work, so acceptance means passing a check the generator did not write for itself.'), ('Continual-learning researcher', "Independence of the validator is the point I would defend most strongly, since a generator grading its own homework converges on leniency. Reviewing validators like production code keeps them evolving as failure modes evolve rather than fossilizing around yesterday's tests. Bounded regeneration with feedback closes the loop without letting iteration run forever, which preserves the pattern's value as a gate rather than an endless polish cycle.")], 'llm-judge': [('Evaluation methodologist', 'LLM-as-Judge grades outputs against a rubric for quality and safety gating, with the judge seeing output plus rubric and context, emitting score with rationale, and gating on threshold with escalation on disagreement. Failures are judge bias across length, position, style and same-family self-preference, and judge injection where content under grading instructs the judge. Protections blind and shuffle candidates with a heterogeneous judge model, wrap graded content as quarantined data, and calibrate the judge against human labels regularly, with evaluator-optimizer and sanitization alongside across general and content work.'), ('Safety researcher', 'Treating graded content as data is the protection that prevents the evaluation itself from becoming an injection path. Blind shuffled presentation plus a different model family reduces both anchoring and self-preference, though neither removes bias entirely, which is why regular calibration against human labels belongs in the record. Threshold gating with escalation on disagreement keeps uncertain judgments in front of people rather than silently passed.')], 'ensemble-verify': [('Evaluation methodologist', 'Ensemble Verification requires multiple heterogeneous verifiers across rules, models and model families to concur before high-impact actions, fanning out to diverse checkers, requiring unanimity or k-of-n with human tiebreak, and recording per-checker verdicts. The failure is homogeneity illusion, where several checkers share training data and one blind spot. Protections include at least one deterministic rule checker plus diverse model families and prompts, with self-consistency and voting parallels as companions across finance and healthcare decisions, so agreement means independent agreement rather than correlated repetition.'), ('Safety researcher', 'The deterministic checker is the anchor I would keep, since purely model-based ensembles can share blind spots while looking redundant. Recording per-checker verdicts makes agreement auditable instead of a single averaged score. Diversity across families and prompts is a cost worth paying where impact is high, because correlated verifiers manufacture confidence without adding safety, which is exactly the homogeneity illusion this record names.')], 'graceful-degradation': [('Safety researcher', 'Graceful Degradation shrinks the action space rather than the safety envelope when confidence or capability drops, detecting model error or tool outage, falling back to read-only or suggest-only modes, and notifying users of reduced mode through a mode controller and capability matrix. The failure is degraded mode still dangerous, where read-only access leaks restricted data. Protections define degraded modes in policy and review them like features, and never widen data rights in degraded mode, with fallback chains and circuit breakers alongside so diminished capability stays inside the same guardrails in general deployments.'), ('Continual-learning researcher', 'Defining degraded modes up front in policy is what makes degradation graceful rather than improvised. My emphasis would be on notification: users acting as if the system is fully capable while it runs diminished will route around the very limits protecting them. Keeping data rights fixed or narrower across modes prevents the quiet expansion that read-only labels can hide, which is why policy review of each mode matters as much as the mode controller itself.')], 'self-healing-replan': [('Safety researcher', 'Self-Healing Replan diagnoses root cause on failure and re-plans under containment so healing does not compound harm, moving from observed failure through bounded diagnosis into containment, re-planning and fix verification, with a failure classifier, containment policy and re-planner. Failures are runaway remediation where the agent worsens an outage by destructive repair, and flapping between oscillating remediations. Protections use a remediation allowlist per system class with destructive actions always gated, cap remediation attempts before paging a human, and enforce change windows with blast-radius caps, tied to incident playbooks across devops and operations.'), ('Continual-learning researcher', 'Bounded diagnosis is theflags discipline I would stress: an agent that investigates forever is itself an incident. Allowlisted remediations plus attempt caps plus human paging turn healing into a finite episode rather than an open-ended campaign. Change windows and blast-radius caps give each repair a place and a size, and verifying the fix before declaring recovery keeps flapping visible instead of letting oscillating repairs masquerade as progress.')], 'loop-detector': [('Evaluation methodologist', 'Loop and Stall Detection fingerprints actions by tool plus argument hash, watches for repeats within a window or absence of state change, then trips the breaker with checkpoint and escalation, through a fingerprinter, progress monitor and breaker hookup. The failure is legitimate repetition flagged as a loop, such as polling tasks tripping the detector. Protections key loop signatures on state delta rather than action repeat alone and let polling tasks declare expected cadence to the monitor, with circuit breakers and bounded execution alongside so genuine stalls stop before cost and side effects compound in general agents.'), ('Safety researcher', 'State delta rather than mere repetition is the distinction that makes this detector usable in production. Fingerprinting gives repeats an observable signature, but only progress monitoring tells a stall from a cadence. Declared polling cadences let legitimate loops identify themselves, which cuts false trips without weakening the trip wire, and hookup to the breaker with checkpointing means detection ends in containment and escalation rather than a log line nobody reads.')]}

PART_DELIB = {'planning': [('Continual-learning researcher', 'Planning is where an agent reasons before it acts, decomposing goals, deliberating over options and correcting itself before touching the world. I see its architectural role as moving risk left: flaws caught in a plan cost a replan, while flaws caught in execution cost side effects. That is why plan stores, verifiers and confidence gates belong beside generation, so reasoning stays reviewable and revisable rather than collapsing into a single forward pass that cannot explain or retract itself.'), ('Memory-systems researcher', 'I agree planning reasons, but I would add that it also stages memory: intermediate steps, candidate branches and verification questions become the working record the rest of the system inspects. Architecturally this means planning needs explicit handoffs to execution, with preconditions revalidated per step and provenance on every claim. Without that staging, reasoning is private text and the loop cannot audit, resume or challenge what the planner decided.'), ('Safety researcher', 'My caution is that eloquent reasoning is not safe reasoning. A fluent plan can rationalize a wrong or risky action, so planning must be paired with independent checks, calibrated confidence and skeptical review before execution. In system terms planning proposes while policy disposes: runtime gates, human approvals and deterministic validators sit outside the planner, which keeps deliberation useful without letting it authorize its own conclusions.')], 'loop': [('Safety researcher', 'The loop controls execution by cycling through observe, think and act with explicit bounds on steps, time, spend and authority. I read it as the system governor: every iteration is metered, every action passes policy, and stop conditions are enforced by the runtime rather than requested of the model. Checkpointing, scoped tools and human gates live here because this is the last place a runaway trajectory can be stopped before its next side effect, which makes loop design the difference between an agent and an incident.'), ('Evaluation methodologist', 'What makes a loop evaluable is that each cycle emits observable state: assembled context, chosen action, executed tool, returned observation and policy verdict. I would design loops so those transitions are logged, metered and comparable across runs, with stall detection and budget exhaustion as first-class terminal states. A loop that cannot report why it stopped, whether by goal, cap, breaker or human halt, cannot be improved, since its failures leave no trace to learn from.'), ('Continual-learning researcher', 'I see the loop as the learning surface: retries, reflections and re-plans all happen inside its iterations, so bounding them matters as much as enabling them. Timeboxing, milestone gates and attempt caps keep adaptation finite, while idempotent resume lets a paused loop continue without duplicating effects. Architecturally the loop should therefore carry both memory of what was tried and restraint on what may be tried next, so persistence never becomes mere repetition.')], 'workflow': [('Evaluation methodologist', 'Workflow orchestrates steps through fixed pre-authored control flows that steer model calls, trading open-ended autonomy for repeatability. Its role is to make behavior predictable: chains with validated boundaries, routers with fallback lanes, fan-outs with concurrency caps, evaluators with iteration bounds. Each shape carries gates between stages so errors are caught at boundaries rather than laundered downstream. I value workflows because their structure is testable: per-step failure rates, route distributions and merge conflicts give reviewers measurable signals about where a pipeline strains.'), ('Safety researcher', 'My defense of fixed flows is that they narrow what the model decides at each point, which narrows what can go wrong. A router with hard-coded safety-critical routes, an orchestrator with scoped worker credentials and spend caps, a pipeline with shared guardrails across fallbacks: each constraint removes a degree of freedom an attacker or a hallucination could exploit. Workflows do not eliminate judgment, but they place it inside channels whose walls are deterministic and whose crossings are logged.'), ('Memory-systems researcher', 'I would add that workflows are also memory discipline: structured outputs, provenance tags and cached node results travel explicitly between stages rather than lingering implicitly in context. Deterministic merges with conflict detection keep parallel branches honest, while per-node budgets rolling up to task budgets keep fan-out affordable. The architectural payoff is composition without amnesia, since each stage hands the next both its result and the record of how that result was reached.')], 'memory': [('Memory-systems researcher', 'Memory remembers across turns, tasks and sessions, spanning working context, short-term episodes and long-term stores such as vectors, graphs and files. Its architectural role is continuity: carrying constraints, decisions, identifiers and unresolved items forward so the agent need not rediscover them. That power needs structure, including priority-aware truncation that never drops policy, provenance and confidence on stored facts, expiry with legal-hold override, and write gates so that what persists was worth persisting rather than whatever happened to be said.'), ('Safety researcher', 'My warning is that memory is also persistence of compromise: a planted instruction, a poisoned precedent or an entombed personal record keeps acting long after the interaction that created it. Treat retrieved content as untrusted data, gate writes with human or high-confidence review, and provide erasure and decay so stale or hostile memories expire. Consolidation below confidence thresholds needs review, and anything resembling a policy bypass must never be consolidated at all.'), ('Evaluation methodologist', 'I read memory as the hardest layer to evaluate because its failures surface far from their cause. A wrong edge becomes canon, a lucky guess is stored as success, a constraint is lost in summarization: each looks fine at write time and harmful at recall. The remedy is ground truth at labeling, verbatim pin-lists for constraints, entailment checks on citations, and audits comparing decisions before and after compression, so memory quality is measured at retrieval rather than assumed at storage.')], 'multiagent': [('Safety researcher', 'Multiagent topologies coordinate specialized agents through supervision, hierarchy, handoff, shared boards, debate and voting, and their architectural role is division of labor under control. The load-bearing choices are authority matrices enforced by runtime rather than prompt, scoped data and tools per worker, allowlisted handoff targets, and humans reserved for irreversible approvals. Without those, coordination multiplies capability and attack surface together: scope bleeds across workers, mid-level agents launder authority, and permissive handoffs invite steering toward the weakest checker.'), ('Evaluation methodologist', 'Debate, voting and red-team pairings earn their keep by surfacing disagreement before production does, but only with design that preserves independence. Blind first rounds prevent anchoring, distinct identities and contexts prevent vote buying through shared context, and judges must document rejected dissent. I would measure groupthink, collusion and moderator capture directly, since a council that converges early on a wrong answer is costlier than any single-agent error it was meant to prevent.'), ('Continual-learning researcher', 'I see coordination cost as the quiet constraint: layers multiply latency and tokens while handoff loops and runaway discussions burn budget without progress. Depth caps, round caps, handoff count caps with auto-escalation and per-debater budgets keep collaboration finite. Append-only boards with per-agent access rules and provenance on every contribution preserve who said what, so the system learns from its collective episodes instead of merging them into an unattributable average.')], 'tools': [('Safety researcher', 'Tools let the agent act on the world through function calls, code execution, browsers, GUIs, sandboxes and registries, which makes tooling the largest side-effect surface in the system. Architecturally every action needs validation beyond syntax, scoped per-caller credentials without ambient authority, dry-run or diff modes before state changes, and disposable sandboxes with default-deny egress. Tool descriptions themselves must be pinned and vetted, since a poisoned registry entry or smuggled tool injects instructions into every client that binds it.'), ('Memory-systems researcher', 'Execution leaves artifacts, and artifacts become memory: stdout, diffs, files and retrieved pages all re-enter context and shape the next decision. That is why results should arrive verbatim through delimited data channels rather than re-interpreted as instructions, and why end-state verification matters more than click fidelity for GUI and browser work. Scoped workspaces, secret scanning on write and read-back distrust keep the scratchpad and the tool channel from becoming durable compromise.'), ('Evaluation methodologist', 'I would judge tooling by containment and fidelity: does the sandbox actually bound network, filesystem and secrets, and does the dry-run diff actually match real apply including secondary effects. Simulation against twins and shadow parity runs give rehearsal without consequence, while mode enforcement in signed responses prevents mode confusion. Heterogeneous fallbacks and promotion gates on eval pass keep capability upgrades honest, since a new tool or skill should prove parity before it earns production rights.')], 'safety': [('Safety researcher', 'Safety constrains what the agent may do through identity, policy, budgets, approvals and content controls enforced outside the model. Its architectural position is a gateway every action crosses: deterministic allow, deny or require-approval evaluated at the tool layer, with default-deny for new action classes and full decision logging. Least privilege, dual control, spend caps and reversibility-first design layer so that each assumes the others may fail. The result is not a safer model but a bounded system, where even a compromised or injected agent meets controls it cannot rewrite.'), ('Evaluation methodologist', 'What distinguishes this safety story is testability: versioned eval harnesses with hold-out attacks, canary rollouts with absolute side-effect caps, drift baselines with owned alerts, and citation verifiers checking entailment rather than existence. Each control emits evidence, from decision logs to redaction records to approval graphs, so reviewers audit behavior rather than intentions. Incident playbooks rehearsed like code and audit trails built for replay turn the rare failure into corpus, closing the loop from protection back into measurement.'), ('Memory-systems researcher', 'The memory dimension of safety is provenance and persistence: every claim tagged to source, every retrieved passage wrapped as untrusted data, every approval and policy verdict chained into a tamper-evident trail. RAG poisoning defense with trust tiers and corroboration, PII vaults with tokenization and erasure, and structured logging with instrumentation-layer redaction keep long-lived stores from becoming long-lived liabilities. Constraining what persists, and remembering exactly where each persisted fact came from, is what lets a system stay safe across sessions rather than within one.'), ('Continual-learning researcher', 'I would frame safety as the envelope inside which learning is allowed. Quotas shared across descendant trees, fan-out caps on delegation, budgets immutable at runtime and degraded tiers with narrower rights all keep adaptation from expanding authority. Abstention with staffed escalation gives uncertainty somewhere honest to go, and kill switches with runtime-only reset plus containment on trip guarantee that learning halts when it must. Safety here is less a feature than a shape: every loop that adapts runs inside bounds it cannot negotiate.')], 'resilience': [('Continual-learning researcher', 'Resilience lets the system survive model, tool and world misbehavior by containing failure and recovering within bounds. Its repertoire is bounded retry with backoff, ordered fallback across tiers, compensation in reverse for partial sagas, replanning under containment, and degraded modes that shrink action space rather than oversight. Attempt caps, remediation allowlists, change windows and human paging keep healing finite. The architectural stance is that failure is normal input: detect it, bound its blast radius, compensate or degrade, verify the fix, and only then continue.'), ('Evaluation methodologist', 'I value resilience because it is observable under stress: validators independent of generators, judges calibrated against human labels, ensembles with deterministic rule checkers, loop signatures keyed on state delta rather than repetition. Each mechanism defines its terminal state explicitly, whether acceptance, escalation or halt, so recovery is measurable rather than hopeful. Keeping per-checker verdicts, serving-tier logs and saga-state histories turns survival into evidence, which is what lets a team distinguish a system that recovered from one that merely continued.'), ('Safety researcher', 'My emphasis is that recovery must never widen authority: degraded tiers get narrower rights, guardrails sit beneath every fallback tier, and destructive remediation stays gated regardless of urgency. Retrying only idempotent or keyed calls prevents rescue from double-charging, while classifying irreversible steps upfront keeps compensation honest about what cannot be undone. Resilience and safety thus meet at containment, since a fallback, retry or replan that escapes its bounds is not recovery but a second incident wearing the first one as cover.')], 'domain': [('Evaluation methodologist', 'Domain playbooks adapt the shared patterns to regulated settings, turning generic guardrails into end-to-end reference architectures per industry. Their role is translation: clinical triage becomes decision-support only with licensed sign-off and deterministic dosage services, trading becomes signal proposal with broker-level caps and staleness gates, procurement becomes draft orders with vendor verification and processor caps. Each playbook names its characteristic failures, from autonomous clinical action to runaway ordering, and pairs them with controls placed at the layer that actually holds under pressure.'), ('Safety researcher', 'What makes playbooks credible is that guardrails travel with them rather than being re-derived per deployment. Support keeps refund caps and account verification, coding keeps sandboxed implementation with human merge gates and secret scanning, SRE keeps remediation allowlists with stateful systems human-gated, research keeps citation resolution against content hashes with abstention over fabrication. The pattern is consistent: diagnose freely where reading is safe, but let money, merges, infrastructure and clinical acts move only through gates the agent cannot own.'), ('Memory-systems researcher', 'I read playbooks as memory with accountability: guideline-grounded suggestions with citations, strategy mandates immutable at runtime, provenance hashed per order, full audit for clinical governance. Each preserves what the domain must remember, from source-quality tiers in research reports to receipt ledgers in procurement, while minimizing what it retains, through tokenized clinical context and vault-mediated identity. Adapting to regulated settings therefore means remembering the right evidence in the right store, retrievable for review long after the run ends.')], 'preface': [('Continual-learning researcher', 'This book treats agent design as a craft of bounded autonomy: give systems room to reason, remember and coordinate, but inside envelopes they cannot renegotiate. Each chapter follows the same arc from pattern through failure to protection, so readers learn not only how a technique works but how it breaks and what holds it. The council voice throughout reflects that stance, with agreement, sharpening and dissent standing in for the review a real deployment needs, since no single perspective sees every failure mode a capable agent can find.'), ('Evaluation methodologist', 'I would ask readers to treat every recommendation here as a hypothesis with an observable signature. Agreement thresholds, abstain rates, route distributions, block rates and drift baselines recur because safety claims should be checkable in logs rather than trusted in prose. The book pairs each control with something to measure and each failure with something to test, so a team can move from reading about guardrails to instrumenting them, and from admiring a design to reproducing its behavior under review.'), ('Safety researcher', 'The premise I would hold highest is enforcement outside the model: policy in middleware rather than prompts, budgets set by callers rather than agents, approvals bound to humans rather than loop participants, sandboxes and egress controls beneath every tier. Models propose while runtimes dispose, and that separation is what lets fallible reasoning drive useful action without being trusted with final authority. Read the chapters that follow as variations on that separation, applied to thinking, memory, tools, teams and recovery alike.')], 'conclusion': [('Safety researcher', 'The closing argument is that safe agency is a property of systems, not of models: scoped identity, deterministic policy, financial and rate bounds, human gates on irreversible acts, content and boundary controls, tamper-evident memory and rehearsed response, layered so each assumes the others may fail. No single control carries the design; their composition does. An agent that inherits this stack can be capable and still be governable, since every path to the world crosses checkpoints its own reasoning cannot move, rename or approve away.'), ('Continual-learning researcher', 'What endures after the details is the discipline of bounded adaptation. Retry, fallback, compensate, degrade, replan, escalate: each is a way to keep going without breaking the envelope, and each stays finite through caps, windows and human handoff. Systems that learn from incidents into eval cases, from drift into rebaselined thresholds, and from near-misses into tighter gates improve without expanding authority. That is the trajectory worth building toward, where experience compounds and blast radius does not.'), ('Evaluation methodologist', 'I would leave readers with measurement as maintenance: replayable trails, per-checker verdicts, serving-tier logs, abstain and block-rate telemetry, canary diffs across config changes. Designs rot as tools, models and threats shift, so the harness, the bench and the drift baselines are not one-time gates but ongoing instruments. A team that keeps those instruments staffed and reviewed will catch its next failure in a dashboard before it meets it in production, which is the quietest victory this book recommends.')]}

APP_DELIB = {'What the Application Is': [('Evaluation methodologist', 'The application is the catalog made interrogable rather than merely readable: a single-page dashboard of plain markup, style and script served by one small standard-library server, rendering diagrams at view time with a vendored engine and no build step or account. Its lifecycle mirrors the book, moving from patterns through failures and protections into live replay and lab-generated guardrail designs. What matters to me is reproducibility of output, since deterministic in-browser analysis plus exportable artifacts means a review discusses the same design tomorrow that it approved today.'), ('Safety researcher', 'I read this chapter as applying the book to its own tool: deterministic analysis instead of model judgment, a gate of lint and integrity tests instead of a build-time checker, a same-origin proxy instead of third-party calls, and a cache instead of a network dependency. The flagship card-charge replay shows layered denial with containment while legitimate orders pass, which demonstrates the defense-in-depth posture the patterns preach. Nothing here enforces on your behalf; it produces designs your runtime must still implement.')], 'Supporting the Agentic Workflow': [('Continual-learning researcher', 'This chapter covers the design half of the agentic loop: the work before, between and after runs where teams choose patterns, write failure modes first, set autonomy and rehearse control flow. I value its spine of four architect questions, each answered by a working surface that leaves an artifact behind, from filtered pattern sets through gap backlogs and blast-radius cascades to readiness scorecards and reviewable decision records. Keeping evidence beside advice is what turns opinions about guards into designs someone can implement and someone else can challenge.'), ('Memory-systems researcher', 'The workflow framing resonates because design memory persists: plans, blueprints, collections and preferences live locally and leave only on export, so iteration accumulates rather than evaporates. Moving from a one-line agent idea to threat model, rollout plan and replayed failure in one session compresses the design loop without surrendering provenance, since every proposal names its records. That continuity lets teams revisit why a guard was chosen long after the meeting that chose it.')], 'Design Principles': [('Safety researcher', 'The principles chapter states the book thesis as self-discipline: safety in deterministic enforcement outside the model, expressed as a short list of constraints visible in files. A rule engine instead of a model for analysis, a gate instead of a build step, plain data instead of a database, one diagram queue instead of concurrent renders, degradation instead of failure: each removes a class of drift between what is read and what runs. I find the inspectability demand load-bearing, since a tool that names its controls must let you open the file and find the line.'), ('Evaluation methodologist', 'What persuades me is that claims are printed as measurements rather than asserted as virtues. Budgets for size and speed, offline behavior verified by visit-then-disconnect, LAN and air-gap operation without registries or remote services: each is catchable when wrong, which is exactly why printing them matters. Designing for degradation keeps the reference useful where networks and backends are absent, so the principles hold under the conditionsört they claim to serve rather than only in the demo.')], 'Architecture': [('Memory-systems researcher', 'The architecture is static files plus one small server: a delivery layer with hardening headers and caching, a shell owning tab switching and registries, feature modules registering into it, phased datasets, live-fetched design documents, a service worker shell cache and an optional same-origin model relay. Nothing compiles, so the architecture read in source is the architecture that runs, with no bundle to unwind or generated output to drift. I like that layer naming guides change, since headers, rules, records and caches each live where a fix in one place cannot silently become a bug in another.'), ('Safety researcher', 'Layering is also a trust argument: deployment copies exactly what the server serves, privilege restrictions arrive via composition rather than behavior change, and any static host can serve the same files. Knowing which layer a control inhabits keeps modifications honest, and the absence of generated code removes an entire class of supply-chain surprise. The shape is deliberately small, which keeps the surface describable and therefore reviewable by people who did not write it.')], 'Privacy: Local Models and Data That Stay Put': [('Safety researcher', 'The privacy posture is structural rather than promised: the page reaches only its own origin, the model reaches only backends on your own network with ordered failover and watchdogs, and everything built stays in local browser storage until export. There is no account, no cloud store and no analytics recipient, so there is no server-side copy to breach. This matters because agent designs map money, personal and health data flows; asking for design help must not leak that map. Local grounded chat keeps questions inside the boundary the design is meant to protect.'), ('Memory-systems researcher', 'Persistence locality is the memory point I would stress: plans and collections rest in origin-scoped storage rather than a shared service, and relayed model replies arrive tagged by backend with deterministic fallback when none answer. Constraining the page client to same-origin connections makes exfiltration a structural impossibility rather than a policy request. For teams drafting threat models and thresholds before shipping, that containment is what lets the tool hold sensitive architecture without becoming its weakest custodian.')], 'Isolation, Hardening and Offline Operation': [('Safety researcher', 'Isolation here spans browser, process, network and time: hardened response headers with strict framing and referrer policy, escaped rendering with strict diagram mode, a minimal non-root container image with read-only filesystem and dropped capabilities, address-scoped publishing with a tailnet-fronted variant, and a precached shell that serves offline after one visit. Each control reads in a file rather than resting on model or vendor trust. I value that offline is a capability rather than a screenshot, since air-gap honesty requires the tool to keep working with the cable out.'), ('Continual-learning researcher', 'The time dimension deserves emphasis: version-bumped cache rotation keeps clients from running stale shells, while network-first with cache fallback keeps same-origin requests alive through outages. Hardening that survives disconnection means lessons learned on connected networks still apply when isolated, which is where many tools quietly fail. Small surface plus explicit bounds on who may talk to the service and what they may do keeps a simple static-plus-server shape genuinely simple under adversarial attention.')], 'Testing the Defenses': [('Evaluation methodologist', 'The Battle Bench turns the catalog on itself by crossing failure scenarios with deployed configurations into derived cases, then executing them through deterministic simulation, golden trace replay or the live local model, with an oracle grading against assertions from each scenario own protections and an adversary probing which control matters most. Runs persist locally and compare across time so model or config changes appear as verdict diffs with explicit regressions. I consider untested controls hypotheses, so moving discovery left into pre-deployment replay is where this bench earns its keep rather than as post-incident forensics.'), ('Safety researcher', 'What closes the loop is coverage honesty: the bench reports what it did not test by severity, derives cases mathematically so new scenarios and configs appear automatically, and saves receipts for review. Adversarial pressure on the configuration finds the load-bearing control instead of assuming all layers hold equally. A design that fails its own scenarios was never a design, only a document, while one that passes still needs production vigilance; the bench distinguishes those states before deployment rather than after harm.')]}
